#[doc = "# Plan for Precise quantities and configurable units\n\n## Affected modules\n`src/quantities.rs` and `src/api.rs` provide a typed, exact conversion endpoint. Recipe integration and local display preferences are implemented; cross-device synchronization is deferred.\n\n## Tasks\n- [x] Design and implement the behaviour for AC 1; add acceptance evidence.\n- [x] Design and implement the behaviour for AC 2; add acceptance evidence.\n- [x] Design and implement the behaviour for AC 3; add acceptance evidence.\n- [x] Design and implement the behaviour for AC 4; add acceptance evidence.\n- [x] Design and implement the behaviour for AC 5; add acceptance evidence.\n\n## Validation\nBefore implementation, derive acceptance tests from each numbered criterion. Include failure cases, household authorization and quantity/provenance checks where applicable. Record commands and results here at delivery.\n\n## First slice evidence\n`cargo test --test quantities --locked` checks exact input retention, dimension-specific conversions, unavailable cross-dimension/spoon conversions and precision limits.\n\n## Integration delivery\nRecipe quantity/evidence persistence and legacy compatibility are implemented. Demo input units and local mass display preference are implemented. `tests/recipes.rs` checks kilogram input round trips across restart and declared piece-mass evidence with identity rejection. Full validation and review remain pending.\n\n## Curated portions\n43 exact USDA SR Legacy reference portions are selected from frozen source records, with original measure descriptions retained. Cross-device preferences are explicitly deferred to the end of the backlog at customer request. They are not part of this delivery.\n\n## Completion\nCustomer requested feature completion and Done status. Acceptance evidence is in validation.md.\nAuthenticated ownership, Git/SQL storage and product clients belong to F09/F18/F22;\ncross-device preference sync is deferred to the end of the backlog, not implemented here.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0003_quantities_units_plan_md {}

#[doc = "# Precise quantities and configurable units\n\nStatus: Done\nPriority: Must\nOrigin: Customer\nMilestone: M1\n\n## User value\nEnter recipes naturally while viewing quantities in personally useful units.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. Given a recipe input in g, kg, ml, l, tsp, tbsp or pieces, the original value and unit are retained with a typed dimension and exact decimal representation.\n2. Given a user allowing only g and kg, recipe quantities display in those units when conversion is known; unavailable conversion is visible and requests ingredient-specific data.\n3. Given a volume-to-mass conversion, it uses a sourced ingredient/state-specific density; piece conversions use a declared piece mass and spoon measures use a named regional standard.\n4. Given scaling by servings, calculations preserve precision until presentation and record estimated conversions; mass never silently equals volume.\n5. Given users with different unit preferences, one user’s display configuration does not rewrite another user’s recipe input.\n\n## First slice\nA typed quantity conversion endpoint retains the submitted decimal string and unit, identifies\nmass/volume/count, and converts exactly between g/kg and ml/l. Piece identity is retained.\nCross-dimension conversion requires ingredient data; spoon conversions require an explicit\nstandard. Results beyond six fractional digits or supported bounds are rejected, never rounded.\nRecipe lines now accept quantity plus optional conversion evidence, persist original input and normalized grams, and verify both on reload. Legacy gram lines remain supported. The demo supports per-line units and local g/kg display preferences. Evidence is user-declared with ingredient/state, HTTPS reference, version, uncertainty, and density or piece mass; spoon input additionally requires a named standard and declared spoon volume. Values are not independently verified provider data.\n\n## Out of scope\nA universal density or undocumented spoon/piece constants.\n\n## UX notes\nSee ux-notes.md and validation.md.\n\n## Links\nRequirement: [F03](../page_docs_requirements_md/index.html). Delivery tasks: [plan.md](../page_specs_0003_quantities_units_plan_md/index.html). Decisions: [adrs.md](../page_specs_0003_quantities_units_adrs_md/index.html).\n\n## Curated reference portions\n43 exact USDA SR Legacy household portions are offered for explicit selection. Stored evidence\nrecords its input unit and source food record ID; applying it to another unit, state or food\nfails validation. Source modifiers distinguish packet/block/cake sizes. Spoon gram weights\nare direct source measures, not inferred ml densities. Cross-device preferences are deferred\nto the end of the backlog at customer request.\n\nCompletion scope: local de/en demo, bounded exact input, sourced/manual conversions and immutable\nrecipe integration. Unsupported exact conversions fail explicitly; source coverage is incremental.\nCross-device preferences are explicitly excluded by the customer.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0003_quantities_units_specification_md {}

#[doc = "# Quantity demo UX\n\nEach ingredient line selects its original input unit. Conversion evidence is an optional\nexpanded section with ingredient-specific mass factor, source URL, version, uncertainty and\nnamed spoon standard/volume. These are user declarations, not validated reference data.\nMissing/invalid evidence blocks calculation and saving while keeping inputs. Numeric evidence\nfactors explicitly use canonical decimal points. Original quantities survive recipe reload.\nA local g/kg display preference affects mass presentation and scaling previews, not saved input.\nNo product UI design or authenticated preference synchronization is included.\n\nMatching ingredients offer an explicit curated reference portion selector. Source descriptions\nremain original English text. Changing ingredient clears the selected conversion. Loaded\nrevisions retain their saved evidence independently of the current reference list.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0003_quantities_units_ux_notes_md {}

#[doc = "# Quantity acceptance evidence\n\n## Completion evidence\nAC coverage: recipe authoring/revisions/restart/conflicts and unknown data are covered by\n`tests/recipes.rs`; original units, exact conversion and unavailable context by quantities\nand recipe tests. All 43 curated portions are verified against frozen sources and round-trip\nthrough saved recipes. Local display preferences do not alter stored input. Scaling tests\ncover non-terminating ratios, repeated target changes, invalid counts, mass bounds, unknown\nnutrition, original-yield retention and restart. Nutrition uses the original rational ratio;\ngram strings alone are rounded for display, never fed back into nutrient computation.\nNo authenticated or cross-device preference claim is made. Existing de/en presentation is\nretained; conversion hints identify required ingredient evidence and spoon standards.\nCompletion commands: import/check verifiers, locale tests, fmt, clippy, nextest, licenses,\naudit, strict rustdoc and MSRV. Final outcomes and CI links are recorded in the completion PR.\n\nFinal local gate passed: 33 nextest tests, six locale tests, catalogue and conversion verifiers,\nfmt, clippy, licenses, audit, strict rustdoc and MSRV 1.85.0.\n\nBrowser completion check passed: missing ml evidence produces an actionable hint; g/kg\nautomatic display shows 1500 g as 1.500000000 kg and 25 g as 25.000000 g without changing\nstored input. The batch-serving editor and proportional preview are explicitly distinguished.\n"]
