#[doc = "# Recipe authoring and scaling\n\nStatus: Done\nPriority: Must\nOrigin: Customer\nMilestone: M1\n\n## User value\nCreate structured recipes that remain useful when portions change.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. Given a recipe, an author can edit title, ingredients from the catalogue, quantities, serving count, instructions and active/passive durations.\n2. Given a new serving count, quantities and per-serving nutrition update while the original yield remains recorded; invalid or zero servings are rejected.\n3. Given ingredient substitutions or unknown ingredients, identity and nutrition gaps are visible instead of silently matched.\n4. Given a saved revision, its ingredients, steps, source, author and calculation inputs can be retrieved consistently.\n\n## Current slice (2026-11-07)\nCustomer-authorized local authoring/persistence with catalogue ingredients and per-serving nutrition:\n- Create, list, retrieve and edit immutable revisions via API and a pragmatic de/en demo (AC 1, 4).\n- Preserve exact gram inputs, title/author attribution, en/de content language, ordered instructions,\n  active/passive seconds and batch servings. Empty steps are allowed for drafts.\n- Pin the referenced catalogue subset and source metadata per revision. Reopening after restart or\n  changing the current catalogue must not change old estimates (AC 3–4).\n- Reject unknown IDs, zero/invalid servings and stale revisions. Known identities without verified\n  composition retain unknown/partial nutrient totals (AC 2 validation, AC 3).\n- Changing servings repartitions the same batch; original revisions remain retrievable. A read-only scaling preview uses the saved revision as its original yield; scaled quantities\n  are rounded half up to 0.000001 g and nutrition uses the exact original serving ratio before display rounding.\n- File storage is local/single-household, loopback-only in the executable, with exclusive locking,\n  bounded versioned records, durable publication, fail-closed recovery and documented backup (F18 slice).\n  No authenticated author/household identity is claimed; shared/hosted access is out of scope.\n\n## Out of scope\nPaid content delivery and external imports.\n\n## UX notes\nSee [demo UX notes](../page_specs_0004_recipe_authoring_ux_notes_md/index.html); product UI remains F22.\n\n## Links\nRequirement: [F04](../page_docs_requirements_md/index.html). Delivery tasks: [plan.md](../page_specs_0004_recipe_authoring_plan_md/index.html). Decisions: [adrs.md](../page_specs_0004_recipe_authoring_adrs_md/index.html).\n\nCompletion scope: local single-household authoring, revision persistence and scaling.\nAuthenticated ownership, alternate storage adapters and product clients remain separate features.\n\nF24 adds explicitly optional author attribution, private household recipe images and compact exact display for the native client; see [daily workflows](../page_specs_0024_nextcloud_daily_workflows_specification_md/index.html).\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0004_recipe_authoring_specification_md {}

#[doc = "# Pragmatic recipe demo UX\n\nScope: disposable demo only, English keyed base with German translations. No product design.\n\nUse the existing ingredient lines/precise grams/servings controls with title, author attribution,\nrecipe text language and optional ordered steps. Each step has instruction and active/passive\nseconds; add/remove use labelled buttons. Inputs have visible labels and numeric constraints.\nNutrition remains prominent in the existing per-serving results and source/unknown tables.\n\nSave creates a new recipe or revision of the loaded identity. Show saved ID/revision in the\nlive status region. List/refresh/load expose an empty state and storage failure state. Load\nand new explicitly say they replace/clear inputs. Failed validation, writes or conflicts keep\ninputs; conflicts require copying edits before reloading/reconciling. Changing form fields\nhides stale estimates. A successful save/load renders nutrition from the saved source snapshot.\nLanguage changes preserve exact amounts and never translate user-authored text automatically.\nA loaded recipe with missing current IDs is shown with its saved nutrition and an explicit\nmessage: restore the catalogue or deliberately replace the missing ingredient before saving.\nThe UI must not silently pick another ingredient. Saving a revision uses the current catalogue;\nthis rule and same-batch serving division appear beside the controls. No authenticated author\nor allergen safety claim, timer scheduling, sharing or proportional scaling is implied.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0004_recipe_authoring_ux_notes_md {}

#[doc = "# Recipe slice validation\n\nDate: 2026-11-07. F04 Done after customer-authorized completion; F18 remains In progress.\n\n## Automated evidence\n- `python3 scripts/generate_docs.py --check` passed.\n- `python3 scripts/import_catalogue.py --check` and `python3 scripts/verify_catalogue.py` passed:\n  unchanged 313 ingredients, 284 profiles, 29 identity-only records and 3,778 numeric values.\n- `node --check src/web/demo.mjs` and `node tests/i18n.test.mjs`: six locale tests passed.\n- `cargo fmt --all --check` and `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings` passed.\n- `cargo nextest run --workspace --locked`: 27 tests passed, none skipped, including seven new\n  durable-recipe acceptance tests and the loopback-only startup check. Startup socket checks\n  require an environment that permits loopback binding; an initial sandboxed run rejected\n  that operation, and the full run with the needed permission passed.\n- `cargo build --release --locked`, `cargo deny check licenses` and `cargo audit` passed.\n- `RUSTDOCFLAGS=\"-D warnings\" cargo doc --workspace --no-deps --locked` passed.\n- `cargo msrv verify -- cargo check --all-targets --locked`: Rust 1.85.0 compatible.\n\n`tests/recipes.rs` verifies create/list/load with exact original gram strings and step durations,\nrestart round trips, historical/latest retrieval, concurrent stale-write rejection, source\nsnapshot stability after catalogue changes, new-revision recalculation, invalid inputs,\nunknown composition, exclusive locks, corrupt/interrupted-store startup rejection and file\npublication failure without overwrite or subsequent writes. `tests/startup.rs` verifies the\nexecutable rejects non-loopback exposure before authentication exists.\n\n## Browser evidence\nUsing temporary storage and the local server, create a German Hafer-Chia-Frühstück recipe\nwith 100,500000 g oats, 25 g chia, two servings and one step (60 active / 300 passive seconds).\nSaving produced revision 1 with 256,22 kcal / 10,55 g protein per serving. Reloading the page\nand loading the saved recipe preserved title, exact gram string, instruction and both durations.\nChanging the same batch to four servings and saving produced revision 2 with 128,11 kcal;\nthe ingredients were not proportionally scaled. Invalid German `1.000` was rejected while\nkeeping input and loaded revision. Switching English preserved `100.500000`, authored German\ntext and durations; reloading restored the saved revision and nutrition. German saved-list,\nload/success/error labels were exercised without product UI design work.\n\n## Review limits\nThis is a local, single-household file slice with self-reported attribution, not authenticated\nownership, Git-backed storage, SQL adapters, timers, product UI or proportional scaling.\nFilesystem failure tests simulate a target collision and interrupted/corrupt files; they do not\nclaim power-loss validation on every filesystem. Linux/local hard-link and fsync support is\nrequired; POST retries after network timeouts need list/history inspection. Operator recovery\nand bounds are documented in the recipe guide. GitHub CI/security evidence belongs in the PR.\n\n## Completion evidence\nAC coverage: recipe authoring/revisions/restart/conflicts and unknown data are covered by\n`tests/recipes.rs`; original units, exact conversion and unavailable context by quantities\nand recipe tests. All 43 curated portions are verified against frozen sources and round-trip\nthrough saved recipes. Local display preferences do not alter stored input. Scaling tests\ncover non-terminating ratios, repeated target changes, invalid counts, mass bounds, unknown\nnutrition, original-yield retention and restart. Nutrition uses the original rational ratio;\ngram strings alone are rounded for display, never fed back into nutrient computation.\nNo authenticated or cross-device preference claim is made. Existing de/en presentation is\nretained; conversion hints identify required ingredient evidence and spoon standards.\nCompletion commands: import/check verifiers, locale tests, fmt, clippy, nextest, licenses,\naudit, strict rustdoc and MSRV. Final outcomes and CI links are recorded in the completion PR.\n\nFinal local gate passed: 33 nextest tests, six locale tests, catalogue and conversion verifiers,\nfmt, clippy, licenses, audit, strict rustdoc and MSRV 1.85.0.\n\nBrowser completion check passed: missing ml evidence produces an actionable hint; g/kg\nautomatic display shows 1500 g as 1.500000000 kg and 25 g as 25.000000 g without changing\nstored input. The batch-serving editor and proportional preview are explicitly distinguished.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0004_recipe_authoring_validation_md {}

