#[doc = "# Plan for Recipe sharing and collections\n\n## Affected modules\nExisting immutable recipes, `AppAPI` household authorization and the native Vue client. Add only\nfeature-owned models/storage/routes needed for collections and sharing; no crates or placeholder adapters.\n\n## Tasks\n- [x] Inspect accepted requirements, current household ownership and immutable recipe boundaries.\n- [x] Resolve the recipient product decision; complete the delivery contract and authorization matrix.\n- [x] Preserve imported source provenance across saving, history loading and revisions, with regressions.\n- [x] Implement revision-checked private collections and pinned recipe references.\n- [x] Implement explicit recipient access and projection-safe imported sharing.\n- [x] Integrate native collection/sharing management and incoming reading with typed EN/DE contracts.\n- [x] Exercise roles, isolation, stale writes, revocation, imported redaction, images and restart.\n- [x] Verify installed Nextcloud behavior, responsive accessibility and cleanup of owned fixtures.\n- [x] Complete all repository/client/container gates; prepare the reviewable PR.\n\nDelivery handoff requires the PR checks to pass at its exact head; this final external state is\nrecorded in the PR rather than recursively committing its own head hash.\n- [x] Design and implement the behaviour for AC 1; add acceptance evidence.\n- [x] Design and implement the behaviour for AC 2; add acceptance evidence.\n- [x] Design and implement the behaviour for AC 3; add acceptance evidence.\n- [x] Design and implement the behaviour for AC 4; add acceptance evidence.\n\n## Validation\nAll acceptance fixtures are synthetic. No private ingredient audit findings are included in public\nfixtures, documentation or PRs. Retained household directories are not read/copied for this task's\ncleanup; only ledger-recorded synthetic households are archived with the single writer stopped.\n\nBackend evidence: `cargo nextest run --workspace --locked` passed 109/109 tests. New regressions cover\npinned collections and restart; role/membership changes; stale and invalid writes; ambiguous persistence;\npersonal publication/revocation; accepted and direct household grants; canonical recipient lookup failure;\nimported projection in summaries/details/scaling/images and retroactive restriction of older revisions.\nThe directory-unavailable fixture returns a deterministic failure rather than relying on TCP teardown.\n\nClient evidence: `npm --prefix clients/nextcloud test` passed 23/23 tests, including strict source-only\ncontracts, unsafe URL rejection, pinned references/duplicates and recipient variants. Strict TypeScript\nproduction build and formatting pass. No dependencies, crates or `AppAPI` scope changes were needed.\n\nThe 17 repository/client gates, strict rustdoc, rootless TCP/Unix container smoke tests and installed\nbrowser acceptance evidence are recorded in [validation.md](../page_specs_0005_sharing_collections_validation_md/index.html). Final PR-head CI is checked\non GitHub before handoff; that status is not inferred from local checks.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0005_sharing_collections_plan_md {}

#[doc = "# Recipe sharing and collections\n\nStatus: Done\nPriority: Must\nOrigin: Customer\nMilestone: M2\n\n## User value\nShare owned recipes and organize collections on a server.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. Given an owned recipe or collection, its owner can save it on the server and select private or explicitly shared access.\n2. Given a recipient without access, recipe content is withheld; revoking a share prevents subsequent server access.\n3. Given an imported recipe, sharing emits only its original source URL and never republishes cached ingredients/instructions.\n4. Given a recipe revision, collections and meal plans retain a defined revision reference rather than changing historical cooking data silently.\n\n## Out of scope\nPayments, federation and claims that downloaded copies can be revoked. Standalone/Flutter client\nintegration remains in F30/F18; automatic source fetching/import is F16.\n\n## UX notes\nUI flows, accessibility, empty/error states and user review points must be specified before Ready.\n\n## Nextcloud delivery contract\nThe customer requested F05 after the merged F34 delivery. Existing recipes belong to households;\nprivate means access stays within the current household roles, not a new individual ownership model.\nThe customer explicitly selected **named Nextcloud accounts and whole households**. Public/anonymous\nlinks and write delegation are not part of this delivery. The contract passed Ready after the\nrecipient decision and is implemented as the Nextcloud delivery below.\n\n- Collections have names, optional descriptions and ordered, explicit `{recipe_id, revision}` entries\n  from the owning household. Source edits never advance those references automatically. Adding,\n  replacing or removing an entry is a revision-checked collection edit.\n- A recipe's explicit imported origin retains its original HTTPS source URL across revisions.\n  Existing records without origin retain their original representation and remain readable.\n  An imported origin cannot be silently converted to owned or replaced by another URL.\n- Sharing must project imported recipes to their source URL before serializing any response,\n  including collection entries, list/search results, previews, scaling and images. No server-side\n  source fetching, cached imported title, instructions, ingredients, image or nutrition is emitted.\n- Recheck current authorization for every detail, collection entry and image request. Revocation\n  removes subsequent server access; neither browser caching nor copied downloads are claimed revocable.\n- Preserve household isolation, frozen ingredient evidence, exact quantities, existing meal-plan\n  references and `AppAPI` authentication/CSRF. Use additive file-backed models; no dependency is needed.\n\n### Access and recipient matrix\n- Household owners manage outbound grants. Owners/editors curate private collections; readers can\n  browse them. Only owners may change a collection's entries while that collection has active or\n  pending external grants. Readers/editors cannot publish additional content to its recipients.\n- A named-account grant gives that account read-only access immediately. A household grant addresses\n  an invitation to a selected account; that contact accepts as the owner of a target household.\n  All current/future members of that target household may read while they remain members. The source\n  owner can also grant directly to another household they own. Reject a grant back to its source home.\n- Pending household invitations expose invitation metadata only, not recipe content. Acceptance\n  explains the household-wide access. Do not publish a directory of other households to select from.\n- A recipient can decline a pending invitation or remove their personal incoming grant. A target\n  household's owner can remove its incoming grant; its editors/readers cannot revoke for everyone.\n- Revocation and collection deletion remove grants atomically. Every incoming read uses current\n  membership/recipient state. No permissions to edit, forward grants or read unrelated household\n  data are conveyed. Anonymous users and unrelated accounts receive no shared content.\n- Collections remain ordered sets of recipe/revision references. Shared collection edits are explicit\n  owner actions; recipe edits never advance published references. Shared recipe details remain pinned.\n  Existing meal plans retain their prior pinned revisions and are not silently changed by collection edits.\n\n### Native workflows\nCollections use a household navigation entry, native lists, search/pagination, a compact editor with\nrecipe/revision selection and explicit save/remove. Recipe and collection details expose Share to the\nowner. A native dialog shows the frozen revision, current grants, recipient type and Nextcloud person\npicker; revocation requires confirmation. Incoming content appears in Shared with me, independently\nof household membership, with pinned recipe reading/scaling and access-checked images. Imported items\nprovide only their source link. Include loading, empty, conflict, error and revoked states; clear\nprotected content after an access failure and do not persist it in browser storage.\n\nImplementation commands: `cargo test --locked --test recipes`; `cargo nextest run --workspace --locked`;\n`cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings`; `npm --prefix clients/nextcloud test`;\n`npm --prefix clients/nextcloud run build`; all repository gates in AGENTS.md.\n\nModel/API code belongs in `src/`, native views/contracts in `clients/nextcloud/src/`, and acceptance\ncoverage in `tests/` and `clients/nextcloud/e2e/`. Follow existing typed errors, exact decimal strings,\nkeyed EN/DE messages and native Nextcloud controls. Never publish private source-audit findings,\nrelax authorization or replace frozen recipe history. Test missing/stale/unauthorized requests,\nimported output redaction and restart as observable behavior, using synthetic fixtures only.\n\n## Links\nRequirement: [F05](../page_docs_requirements_md/index.html). Delivery tasks: [plan.md](../page_specs_0005_sharing_collections_plan_md/index.html). Decisions: [adrs.md](../page_specs_0005_sharing_collections_adrs_md/index.html).\n\n\n## Acceptance evidence\nThe Nextcloud delivery meets AC 1–4. See [validation.md](../page_specs_0005_sharing_collections_validation_md/index.html) for the acceptance trace,\n109 backend tests, 23 client tests, installed browser scenarios and container/privacy boundaries.\nFinal candidate and exact-head CI results are retained in the reviewable pull request.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0005_sharing_collections_specification_md {}

#[doc = "# Native recipe collections and sharing\n\nUse the existing Nextcloud shell, theme tokens, typography and compact record lists. Add a household\nCollections destination and a Share action in recipe/collection details. A private collection starts\nwith a clear empty state and an Add recipe action; choose a recipe and explicit saved revision.\nShow revision labels, ordered entries and straightforward remove actions. Retain drafts on conflict\nand recover with reload; do not discard work after a failed save.\n\nKeep sharing management separate from recipe editing. Show the exact revision and recipients before\napplying a grant. The household owner controls access; reader/editor behavior must remain explicit.\nThe customer chose accounts and households. Household invitations address a contact, who accepts as\nthe owner of a destination household; show that all its current/future members gain read access.\nOffer directly owned destination households without exposing other households' names. An incoming Shared with me destination\nshould work without household membership and must not expose source household navigation.\n\nImported entries show an Original recipe link rather than cached recipe content. Explain that the\nsource link is shared, with no external fetch, embedded image or preview. Empty/error/revoked states\nmust clear protected content. Use native dialogs, visible labels, keyboard focus restoration, busy\nstates and confirmation for removal/revocation. Check EN/DE, system light/dark and 320/390/1440 px\nwith scoped axe scans and screenshots of owned synthetic fixtures.\n\nTaste is applied to alignment, spacing, hierarchy and visual consistency within the existing shell;\nits marketing-page layouts/assets/gates do not replace Nextcloud components. UI/UX Pro Max's verified\nconfirmation/success-feedback guidance applies. Its optional form-library recommendation is unnecessary\nfor these bounded forms: keep the existing strict Zod contracts and native controls. Preserve dirty\ndrafts, exact quantities and permission states over generic styling recommendations.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0005_sharing_collections_ux_notes_md {}

#[doc = "# F05 acceptance evidence\n\n## Automated contract checks\n`cargo nextest run --workspace --locked`: **109 passed, 0 skipped**.\n`npm --prefix clients/nextcloud test`: **23 passed**.\n\n| Acceptance | Observable evidence |\n|---|---|\n| 1: private and explicit sharing | Private collection creation/editing; source-owner-only sharing; immediate account grants, addressed household acceptance, direct owned-household grants; typed native management/incoming views |\n| 2: access and revocation | Unrelated/anonymous access denied; current membership/role checks; no source household access for recipients; owner-only editing of shared collections; removed entries and collection deletion revoke access; pinned images retain MIME/no-sniff/no-store; restart and failed storage/lookup checks |\n| 3: imported source URL only | Sticky HTTPS provenance, unsafe URL rejection, strict client source-only schema, no cached content in shared summaries/details/scaling/images, and retroactive restriction of older shared revisions without rewriting history |\n| 4: explicit revisions | Collection references and personal publication remain pinned after source edits; explicit revision publication; historical collection reading with Open current revision; exact existing serving scaling and frozen ingredient evidence; existing meal-plan revision regressions remain green |\n\nFocused regressions live in `tests/recipes.rs`, `src/exapp/library_tests.rs`,\n`src/exapp/sharing_tests.rs`, `src/exapp/sharing_collection_tests.rs` and\n`clients/nextcloud/tests/library-api.test.ts`. Fixtures contain no private audit findings.\n\n## Repository and client gates\nAll commands passed:\n\n```sh\npython3 scripts/generate_docs.py --check\npython3 scripts/import_catalogue.py --check\npython3 scripts/verify_catalogue.py\npython3 scripts/import_nutrition_estimates.py --check\npython3 scripts/verify_nutrition_estimates.py\npython3 scripts/verify_conversions.py\npython3 scripts/verify_allergens.py\nnode --test tests/i18n.test.mjs\ncargo fmt --all --check\ncargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings\ncargo nextest run --workspace --locked\ncargo deny check licenses\ncargo audit\nnpm --prefix clients/nextcloud run format:check\nnpm --prefix clients/nextcloud test\nnpm --prefix clients/nextcloud run build\nnpm --prefix clients/nextcloud audit --audit-level=moderate\nRUSTDOCFLAGS='-D warnings' cargo doc --workspace --no-deps --locked\n```\n\nThe production build transforms 861 modules and produces about 167 kB CSS (24 kB gzip) and\n1.44 MB JS (442 kB gzip). These are build output sizes, not measured load-time claims.\nNo runtime dependencies or crates were added. Existing Zod annotation build notices do not affect\nstrict type checking. No global design reset, fonts or theme palette were introduced.\n\n## Container and installed checks\n`python3 scripts/test_exapp_container.py --image mealshop.local/mealshop:sharing-collections`\npassed both isolated rootless TCP and Unix-socket modes. Alongside lifecycle, authentication, CSRF,\nassets, private files, shopping and cooking, the smoke test creates a collection, grants a canonical\naccount read access, denies source-household traversal, corrects the recipe's imported origin and\nverifies source-only access to its older pinned revision before revoking the grant. `library.json`\nremains mode 0600.\n\nThe F05 image is installed in the existing Nextcloud 35.0.2 test deployment using its existing `AppAPI`\nregistration, secret, internal URL and data volume. A single writer is maintained during replacement.\nAll 23 existing/new browser scenarios have been exercised on the installed image. The first complete\nsweep passed 21, hit one Nextcloud SQLite `database is locked` error during a synthetic recipient login,\nand skipped the final serial scenario in that file. The test instance used `DELETE` journal mode.\nAfter switching its supported `sqlite.journal_mode` setting to `WAL` and verifying the actual mode with\n`PRAGMA journal_mode`, all three scenarios in `nextcloud.spec.ts` passed (48.8 s). This is a test-environment\nchange, not a Mealshop database migration. The F05 scenarios passed in that installed sweep (24.8/35.2 s).\n\nThe closing full sweep, final-candidate F05 rerun, image identity and exact-head CI are recorded in the PR.\nSynthetic households are selected from the fixture ledger, checked against synthetic recipe/collection\nidentities and archived with the single writer stopped. Retained household directories are neither read\nnor copied by this cleanup. Their membership entries and monotonic household identity counter are kept.\nNo broad original-file checksum audit is claimed.\n\n## Browser coverage\n`clients/nextcloud/e2e/sharing.spec.ts` covers two real Nextcloud accounts: personal revision\npublication/scaling/revocation, private collection editing/reordering and focused search, historical\nreading, native contact selection, household acceptance/removal, imported-source-only collection\nentries, revoked-content clearing and browser exceptions. It checks EN/DE, system light/dark,\n1440/390/320 px, no page overflow and scoped WCAG 2.2 AA axe scans. Native source controls are exercised\nby keyboard. Browser evidence is scoped automated testing, not a blanket accessibility certification.\nScreenshots remain local ignored artifacts of owned synthetic data.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0005_sharing_collections_validation_md {}

