#[doc = "# F06 delivery plan\n\n## Implemented slice\n- [x] AC1: exact recipe quantities and explicit selected meal-plan slots; pinned revisions, strict dimensions.\n- [x] AC2: contributor/receipt disclosure and editable unrelated goods.\n- [x] AC3: revision-checked source edits preserve immutable purchases and manual sources.\n- [x] AC4: native checkboxes, 48px touch areas, focused shopping mode, responsive layouts.\n\n## Evidence\n`cargo test --locked --test shopping`: four protected API integration tests pass, including role denial,\nconflicts, restart recovery, unit separation, rescaling and selected plan synchronization.\n`npm run build` passes with strict Vue/`TypeScript` checking. The embedded Nextcloud browser contract\nis `clients/nextcloud/e2e/shopping.spec.ts`; final integrated results are recorded in the combined delivery.\n\n## Boundaries\nPurchased receipts are not an inventory ledger. Each recipe source owns its purchases; unused amounts\nare not automatically reassigned to another source. Capacity/ambiguous writes fail closed.\n\nFinal delivery: all four ACs pass the API/native browser acceptance mapping in validation.md.\nThe combined suite passes 16/16, followed by 4/4 final-image shopping/dialog checks.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0006_shopping_list_plan_md {}

#[doc = "# Shopping lists and recipe provenance\n\nStatus: Done\nPriority: Must\nOrigin: Customer\nMilestone: M2\n\n## User value\nShop from meal plans while keeping track of why each item is needed.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. Given selected recipes and serving counts, a list aggregates compatible ingredient quantities without losing contributing recipe/plan references.\n2. Given a listed item, the household can inspect contributing recipes and quantities; it can also add unrelated groceries or household goods.\n3. Given removal or rescaling of a recipe, only its unpurchased contribution changes and manually added contributions remain.\n4. Given shopping mode, large touch targets support fast checking/unchecking in a Bring-inspired interaction with a distinct visual design.\n\n## Out of scope\nAutomatic shop ordering and barcode lookup, specified separately.\n\n## UX notes\nUI flows, accessibility, empty/error states and user review points must be specified before Ready.\n\n## Links\nRequirement: [F06](../page_docs_requirements_md/index.html). Delivery tasks: [plan.md](../page_specs_0006_shopping_list_plan_md/index.html). Decisions: [adrs.md](../page_specs_0006_shopping_list_adrs_md/index.html).\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0006_shopping_list_specification_md {}

#[doc = "# Native shopping experience\n\nOne household shopping destination, with recipe/meal-plan contributions and manually entered goods.\nIn shopping mode, a large named checkbox completes the remaining contributions of an item; purchased\nitems move to a separate disclosure and can be unchecked. Partial purchases remain visible. Show exact\nbase quantities (g, ml, pieces), with original input/package units in contributor details.\n\nRecipes are pinned by revision and servings. Users explicitly add/update/remove a recipe source, or\nreview selected meal slots before synchronizing them. Updating/removing sources changes only outstanding\nrequirements: purchased receipts retain their original recipe/package provenance. Manual contributions\nare independent. No implicit stock reallocation or ml-to-g conversion.\n\nUse official Nextcloud controls, visible labels, predictable focus, pending-action locks, concise success\nand recoverable conflict feedback. Include accessible empty/read-only/error/loading states, de/en keyed\nmessages, native themes and responsive layouts. Never run browser tests against customer households.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0006_shopping_list_ux_notes_md {}

#[doc = "# Combined F06/F07/F08 evidence\n\nEnvironment: Nextcloud 35.0.2, `AppAPI` 35.0.0, Vue 3, @nextcloud/vue 9.14.1; real embedded local test\ninstallation. Synthetic households are recorded/archived; customer data is never a test write target.\n\n## Acceptance mapping\n| Contract | Observable verification |\n|---|---|\n| F06 AC1–3 | tests/shopping.rs: exact units, aggregation, selected plan revisions, immutable purchases, rescale/remove, extras and restart |\n| F06 AC4 | e2e/shopping.spec.ts: shopping mode, 1440/768/390/320 bounds, axe WCAG tags and native touch targets |\n| F07 AC1/4 | Protected API and embedded preferences/fallback/manual-order flow; unchanged source quantities/provenance |\n| F07 AC2/3/5 | Three-session threshold, manual precedence, correction exclusion, opt-in, inspect/reset/disable and restart |\n| F08 AC1–3 | GTIN/check digits, package snapshots, explicit match confirmation, denied-camera/failed-provider manual continuation |\n| F08 AC4 | Bounded provider records, no nutrition/match inference, forged-candidate rejection; consent denial has no file/network mutation |\n| F21/F22 | Native locale tests and embedded suite; original cross-client criteria retained verbatim in F29/F30 |\n\n## Automated results\n- Required catalogue import/verifier and demo i18n checks pass.\n- `cargo nextest run --workspace --locked`: 67 tests pass; strict workspace Clippy, formatting, licences and audit pass.\n- `npm --prefix clients/nextcloud run test`: 10 tests pass; strict Vue build and whole-client formatting pass.\n- Full npm audit: zero vulnerabilities; no dependency or crate additions.\n- Isolated rootless container tests pass for TCP and Unix socket, including shopping/products and mode-0600 storage.\n- Mutation check: removing the shopping revision guard fails the stale-write acceptance test; original source restored.\n- Complete embedded suite on the deployed container: 16/16 pass, including roles/revocation, previous authoring/planning/ingredient views, light/dark/reduced motion, responsive bounds and axe checks.\n- Scan-adapter tests use a local synthetic `MediaStream` and native API stub; denied permission and failed lookup retain full manual entry.\n- F29/F30 acceptance criteria compare byte-for-byte with the original F21/F22 criterion sections.\n- Final image presentation checks: 4/4 shopping browser contracts pass, including product-dialog responsive bounds at 390/320/1440 and axe WCAG checks. Screenshots were inspected locally.\n- Upgrade and restart: all authenticated API snapshots and 24 persistent files remain identical; one referenced image verified.\n- Final cleanup: only the retained customer household remains; own recipe access works, all retained files equal the initial pre-test backup, 19 household slots are free, monotonic IDs are preserved.\n- Final deployed local image ID: d976a819339f; no production deployment or external publication. Physical mobile camera\nhardware and global provider coverage are outside this environment. Simulated denied-camera and\nsynthetic provider records establish fallback/data handling, not universal optical recognition.\n\n## Data cleanup\nThe previous 36 confirmed browser households were archived with a complete private backup. Customer\nfiles were retained byte-identically. New fixtures have a private ID ledger plus content checks;\nunrecognized/customer content is excluded. No credentials/private household content enter the PR.\n\n## Native tile refinement (F32)\nThe existing source/quantity/permission contracts remain intact. Searchable native tiles, exact inline\nentry, check/undo, item details and their real embedded acceptance are recorded in\n[F32 validation](../page_specs_0032_visual_shopping_validation_md/index.html). No endpoint or persisted model changed.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0006_shopping_list_validation_md {}

