#[doc = "# Delivery plan: shops and optional order learning\n\n- [x] AC1: persistent named shops, per-ingredient first/second choices and keyboard/touch manual order.\n- [x] AC2: explicit opt-in completed sessions; corrections invalidate session observations.\n- [x] AC3: at least three valid multi-item sessions before learned order; manual overrides win.\n- [x] AC4: assignment/fallback changes only metadata, preserving quantities and source snapshots.\n- [x] AC5: inspect/discard/reset/disable sessions independently of shopping data.\n\n## Evidence\nSee [combined validation](../page_specs_0006_shopping_list_validation_md/index.html). Backend acceptance contracts are in\n`tests/shopping.rs`, provider/GTIN boundary tests in `src/shopping/lookup.rs`, native browser flows\nin `clients/nextcloud/e2e/shopping.spec.ts`.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0007_shops_order_learning_plan_md {}

#[doc = "# Preferred shops and learned shopping order\n\nStatus: Done\nPriority: Should\nOrigin: Customer\nMilestone: M2\n\n## User value\nFind ingredients at the right shop and walk the shop in a useful order.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. Given an ingredient, a household can set first and second choice shops and manually edit shop-specific aisle ordering.\n2. Given live check-off events, an opt-in learner derives order separately per shop from actual shopping sessions; undo/corrections do not become confident observations.\n3. Given sparse history, a manual or default order works and the learned order is labelled uncertain; manual overrides take precedence.\n4. Given a shop change or missing stock, items can move to a fallback shop without losing quantities or recipe provenance.\n5. Given learning history, a household can inspect, reset and disable it without losing its shopping list.\n\n## Out of scope\nLocation surveillance or unconsented cross-household training.\n\n## UX notes\nUI flows, accessibility, empty/error states and user review points must be specified before Ready.\n\n## Links\nRequirement: [F07](../page_docs_requirements_md/index.html). Delivery tasks: [plan.md](../page_specs_0007_shops_order_learning_plan_md/index.html). Decisions: [adrs.md](../page_specs_0007_shops_order_learning_adrs_md/index.html).\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0007_shops_order_learning_specification_md {}

#[doc = "# Shops and optional learning\n\nShop filtering and shopping sessions belong in the shopping view. Shop management and ingredient first/\nsecond choice preferences are explicit. Move an unavailable item to its fallback without changing any\nquantity/source. Shop-specific up/down controls provide a keyboard/touch alternative to dragging.\n\nLearning is disabled by default. Starting an opted-in session names the shop and says that check-off\norder is recorded locally for this household. Only completed sessions count; unchecks/corrections\ninvalidate observations. At least three valid sessions per item are needed before a learned position\nis applied. Show manual/default/uncertain/learned status and sample counts. Manual ordering wins.\n\nHistory can be inspected, reset and disabled independently of shopping data. No location access,\ncross-household data, dietary inference or remote model. Reflect loading/failure/conflict states.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0007_shops_order_learning_ux_notes_md {}

