#[doc = "# Multi-day bread, rolls and pizza scheduling\n\nStatus: Done\nPriority: Should\nOrigin: Customer\nMilestone: M3\n\n## User value\nPrepare long-fermentation dough around a target serving time.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. Given bread/roll/pizza/baguette steps across several days, dependencies and active/passive time windows produce a reviewable schedule.\n2. Given preheating, stretch-and-fold cycles and fermentation stages, reminders name the action and required equipment before it is due.\n3. Given a delayed step or changed bake time, dependent reminders are recalculated with a preview and temperature/fermentation uncertainty is explicit.\n4. Given a multi-day schedule crossing a daylight-saving transition, local-time presentation and stored deadlines remain consistent.\n\n## Out of scope\nGuaranteed fermentation outcomes or copying a third-party recipe collection.\n\n## UX notes\nUI flows, accessibility, empty/error states and user review points must be specified before Ready.\n\n## Links\nRequirement: [F13](../page_docs_requirements_md/index.html). Delivery tasks: [plan.md](../page_specs_0013_bread_schedules_plan_md/index.html). Decisions: [adrs.md](../page_specs_0013_bread_schedules_adrs_md/index.html).\n\nAcceptance evidence: [validation.md](../page_specs_0013_bread_schedules_validation_md/index.html).\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0013_bread_schedules_specification_md {}

#[doc = "# Native cooking and scheduling UX\n\nNextcloud components/tokens, existing typography and navigation remain authoritative. UX-UI-Max-Pro\nguides progressive disclosure, recovery and focus; Taste guides alignment, rhythm and screenshot review.\nIts marketing heroes, own palettes/fonts, global resets, shaders and navigation are explicitly excluded\nby the customer hierarchy. Existing native recipe/planning screens are the visual reference.\n\nCooking has a household list and one focus view per pinned recipe instance. Ready actions and overdue\ntimers come first; other stages remain visible in dependency order. One action starts a named preset timer.\nPause/resume/complete are large named controls. A paused/overdue state is textual, not only color.\nCountdowns do not announce every second; meaningful phase/status changes use a polite status region.\n\nPlanning starts from real recipe steps with explicit additional stages. Main fields are name, durations\nand dependencies; equipment, repeated cycles, passive-time bounds and uncertainty expand when needed.\nA target local date/time and IANA zone are visible together. Repeated civil times require a choice; gaps\nrequire a corrected time. No duration or fermentation advice is invented.\n\nReview shows old/new local times with offsets, dependencies, equipment, start windows, overlaps and\nmissed targets. Apply requires an explicit review; changing input invalidates the preview. Existing timers\ncontinue while a draft is edited. Polling never replaces draft input or focus. Stale revisions preserve\ninput and offer reload/review. Cancelling a draft requires discard only when it changed.\n\nNotifications default off. An explicit self-subscription explains Nextcloud acceptance versus actual\ndevice delivery. Denied/unsupported browser permission, failed/unknown attempts, acknowledgements and\nmissed actions remain visible. Requests never silently retry an ambiguous notification outcome. Offline\nstate disables mutations while retaining elapsed deadlines. Empty/loading/error/read-only states explain\nwhat to do next. Verify real embedded routes, keyboard, 320/390/768/1440, light/dark and axe.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0013_bread_schedules_ux_notes_md {}

#[doc = "# F13 acceptance evidence\n\nScope: recipe-derived native Nextcloud baking plans; all original acceptance criteria remain unchanged.\n\n| AC | Evidence |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | `cooking::plan::tests::dependency_windows_cycles_and_dst_use_absolute_elapsed_time` verifies multi-day dependencies, repeated occurrences with waits and shortest/longest passive bounds. API test `multiday_replans_save_the_reviewed_deadlines_and_keep_delays_across_later_changes` proves preview causes no durable write and apply stores exactly the reviewed schedule. |\n| 2 | Action/equipment/lead times are explicit stage fields; preparation, planned-start, active-phase and elapsed events share the durable outbox. Delivery tests verify recipient, action, equipment and event identity without inventing a baking preset or a fermentation outcome. |\n| 3 | Replan tests fix actual completed work, preserve explicit delays across later target changes and flag missed targets, active overlaps and equipment overlaps. Native target-change review presents old/new local times; arbitrary timers and pending starts use the same review/apply boundary. Unspecified conditions remain unknown. |\n| 4 | Jiff resolves IANA zones with bundled data. Unit/API tests cross spring and autumn offsets, reject nonexistent local times and require an explicit fold choice. Browser creates a multi-day plan across the Europe/Berlin autumn transition, reviews both UTC offsets and changes its target. |\n\nShared quality evidence and notification limitations: [F12 validation](../page_specs_0012_guided_cooking_validation_md/index.html).\nAdditional regression tests enforce repeated-step waits from actual completion and preserve explicit\nstart delays. A paused phase projects a resume now even with a future baking target.\n\nNo temperature sensor, biological prediction, commercial recipe collection, standalone shell or Flutter\nalarm implementation is implied. See [ADR 0016](../page_docs_adr_0016_durable_cooking_and_civil_time_md/index.html)\nand the [operator/user guide](../page_docs_guides_cooking_md/index.html).\n"]
