#[doc = "# F15 delivery plan\n\n1. Extend the existing atomic shopping state with exact lots, immutable movement/operation receipts,\n   held/consumed/released source allocations and manually recorded offers. Test durable validation,\n   dimensions, insufficient stock, atomic failures, reversal and idempotent restart first.\n2. Wire authenticated read/preview/confirm routes, current catalogue/profiles/completed cooking and\n   shopping receipts; derive purchase reduction and preserve source facts under edits/check-off.\n3. Deliver native inventory and offer views plus shopping/cooking entry points, typed contracts,\n   review/retry/discard and keyed EN/DE messages.\n4. Verify every criterion in isolated backend and real Nextcloud owner/reader flows, screenshots,\n   responsive/accessibility checks, installed restart/rootless transports; clean only owned synthetic\n   households, run mandatory gates and complete one PR against main.\n\n- [x] Read requirements/spec and existing shopping, quantity, planning, cooking and role boundaries.\n- [x] Record the delivery contract, UX and atomicity decision.\n- [x] AC 1: exact lots, metadata/corrections/archive and durable source records.\n- [x] AC 2: reviewed reservations and explicit remaining purchase projection.\n- [x] AC 3: purchase/completed-cooking booking, reversal and idempotent recovery.\n- [x] AC 4: manual offers, package/price/source/validity and current dietary constraints.\n- [x] Native integration, local gates, installed transport/restart evidence and synthetic cleanup.\n\nCurrent-head CI is an external handoff gate: all eleven PR checks must pass before the PR is marked\nready and handed back. Its authoritative record is the PR Checks tab.\n\nImplementation uses no new dependencies and remains within the existing shopping transaction. The\nreview corrected movement pagination, preserved reviews across locale-only quantity changes and\nguarded delayed booking/refresh responses. See [validation.md](../page_specs_0015_inventory_offers_validation_md/index.html) for exact evidence.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0015_inventory_offers_plan_md {}

#[doc = "# Inventory and shopping offers\n\nStatus: Done\nPriority: Should\nOrigin: Customer\nMilestone: M3\n\n## User value\nUse existing stock and relevant offers in planning and shopping.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. Given household stock, quantity, unit, location and optional expiry/batch can be recorded and corrected.\n2. Given a plan/list, available stock can reduce the proposed purchase with a visible reservation; a plan alone never consumes stock.\n3. Given confirmed cooking/purchases, stock updates are reviewable and idempotent; corrections reverse the relevant movement.\n4. Given a shop offer, shop, product/ingredient match, price, package size, validity and source are recorded; dietary exclusions still win.\n\n## Out of scope\nUnlicensed offer scraping or automated purchasing.\n\n## UX notes\nSee [ux-notes.md](../page_specs_0015_inventory_offers_ux_notes_md/index.html) for native entry, review, recovery and accessibility.\n\n## Links\nRequirement: [F15](../page_docs_requirements_md/index.html). Delivery tasks: [plan.md](../page_specs_0015_inventory_offers_plan_md/index.html). Decisions: [adrs.md](../page_specs_0015_inventory_offers_adrs_md/index.html).\n\n## Nextcloud delivery contract\n- Manual lots retain original exact quantity/unit, explicit ingredient/product or unmatched identity,\n  location, optional batch/date and append-only physical movement history. Correction records the\n  observed remaining quantity and reason; used identities/units are immutable and empty lots archive.\n- Shopping/plan exports reserve exact compatible lots after review, with dated lots ordered first;\n  passed dates are not proposed. Unknown dates are explicit. No mass/volume/count assumptions.\n- Source changes release obsolete holds. Held stock reduces proposed purchases; confirmed usage\n  remains visibly distinct from purchased receipts. Plans/check-off alone never debit physical stock.\n- Reviewed purchased receipts add lots; completed cooking books reviewed actual available inputs.\n  Incomplete coverage is explicit. Reversals reference the original movement, append its opposite\n  and cannot create negative balances or consume another reservation.\n- Stable actor-bound operation keys, identical payload checks and expected shopping revisions are\n  atomically persisted with effects. Readers cannot mutate; definite conflicts retain local drafts\n  and ambiguous responses retry the immutable confirmed request.\n- Offers are manually entered with shop, explicit binding, positive exact price (EUR/GBP/USD/CHF),\n  positive package quantity, inclusive date range and a source label/optional HTTPS link. Optional\n  product bindings retain their reviewed snapshot. Adding offers checks the explicit shopping date\n  and current intended profiles; exclusions block it. There is no provider/scraping or substitution.\n- Preserve old snapshots/default-empty state, the existing 4 MiB cap and canonical private publication.\n  Bound lots/offers/allocations/movements/receipts and validate persisted references on restart.\n\nDecisions: [ADR 0024](../page_docs_adr_0024_household_stock_and_offers_md/index.html). Complete AC 1–4 with native\nowner/reader tests, durable restart/failure tests, required gates and synthetic-only test cleanup.\n\n## Acceptance evidence\n\nAC 1–4 are implemented and verified in the native Nextcloud delivery. See [validation.md](../page_specs_0015_inventory_offers_validation_md/index.html)\nfor isolated domain tests, all installed browser scenarios, transport/restart/cleanup evidence and the\nmandatory current-head CI boundary. No provider or automatic purchasing is implied.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0015_inventory_offers_specification_md {}

#[doc = "# Native household stock and offers\n\nUse the existing Nextcloud shell, components, MDI icons, theme tokens and EN/DE messages. This is a\nhousehold tool, not a marketing page: Taste informs alignment, density and plain action labels;\nits hero/palette/font/effect/navigation recipes do not apply. UX-UI Pro Max informs visible labels,\nconfirmation, keyboard order and recovery.\n\nInventory opens with searchable lots and exact remaining/reserved/available quantities, location,\nbatch and optional date. Add a lot in context; metadata editing, observed-quantity correction and\narchive are separate actions. Empty stock invites entry, never implies missing food is zero.\n\nShopping links to a stock review: select contributions and use date, preview exact lot reservations\nand remaining purchases, then explicitly confirm. Reserving never consumes stock. Held, used and\nreleased allocations are named; covered rows cannot be mistaken for purchased tiles. Source changes\nrelease obsolete holds; physical consumption remains an explicit historical fact.\n\nPurchase receipt entry and completed-cooking consumption each preview before/after balances and\nsource references. Exact matching uses IDs and dimensions, not names or universal density. Missing\nstock stays visible as unbooked requirements. History supports explicit reversal with a reason;\nnegative or over-reserved balances are blocked with recovery guidance.\n\nOffers have shop, explicit ingredient/product binding, package quantity, price/currency, date range\nand user-entered source. Default to a labelled shopping date and all household profiles; a writer\ncan choose intended profiles. Known exclusions block adding to shopping; unknown safety needs review.\nNo scraping, automatic substitutions, shopping or stock booking.\n\nUse one labelled review surface with a before/after summary. Disable repeated submits; an ambiguous\nsubmission freezes its body/key for retry. Definite conflicts retain edits and require reload/review.\nLeaving drafts asks explicitly. Readers can inspect but cannot preview/confirm mutations. Verify real\nNextcloud routes, keyboard/focus, EN/DE, light/dark, reduced motion and 1440/390/320 px with axe/screens.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0015_inventory_offers_ux_notes_md {}

#[doc = "# F15 validation evidence\n\nDate: 2026-11-12. Installed acceptance is complete; the current-head PR Checks tab is authoritative\nfor the mandatory eleven-check CI handoff gate. No check is waived.\nThe delivery covers exact stock and manually entered offers, not a provider integration or scraping.\n\n## Acceptance trace\n\n| Criterion | Evidence |\n| --- | --- |\n| AC 1: exact lots and corrections | `src/inventory/{lots,ledger,validation}.rs`, foundation/API tests and native add/count-to-zero/archive flow. Original quantity/unit, frozen identity, location, batch, date and append-only reasoned corrections survive reload. |\n| AC 2: visible reservations | `src/inventory/allocations.rs`, shopping projection/source reconciliation tests and native reserved/covered-by-stock flow. Exact dimensions, expiry/use date, source changes and exact product identity are checked. Plans and check-off never debit physical stock. |\n| AC 3: explicit physical bookings | `src/inventory/{purchases,cooking,operations}.rs`, concurrent/restarted retry and publication-failure tests; native purchase/cooking/reversal/ambiguous-response flow. Partial consumption remains unbooked; another source's holds cannot be used. |\n| AC 4: manual offers | `src/inventory/offers.rs`, current-profile exclusion and frozen source tests; native localized price, package, validity, source and reviewed add flow. A profile change after preview blocks confirmation; old shopping facts survive editing/archive. |\n\nTen isolated API tests plus two foundation tests cover exact normalization, old/default-empty state,\nprivate publication, concurrency, restart, changed-key conflicts, corruption and ambiguous publication,\ndimensions, passed dates, product GTIN matching, source changes, incomplete cooking, reverse/rebook,\ncurrent dietary constraints and actual movement pagination. A failed/uncertain store refuses reads,\nnew writes and replays until recovery; no stale pre-publication balance is returned as current.\n\n## Local gates and review\n\nThe complete 23-command local gate passed: catalogue/nutrition/conversion/allergen checks; demo syntax\nand i18n; fmt, Clippy with warnings denied, **166/166** nextest tests, unchanged licence policy and\nadvisory audit; native Prettier, **33/33** Vitest tests, strict Vue/TypeScript/Vite and zero-vulnerability\nnpm audit; generated docs/MCP schema, **5/5** Python bridge tests, official MCP SDK modern HTTP and\nmodern/legacy stdio interoperability, locked debug build and strict rustdoc. The last layout refinement\nwas rechecked with Prettier, all 33 client tests and the production build.\n\n`cargo +1.85.0 check --workspace --all-targets --locked` passes. The actual compiler in the unchanged\npinned image is verified as **rustc 1.99.1**; the old CI display label mentioning 1.85 is not evidence of\nthat image's compiler. No new runtime dependency, advisory exception or loosened lint is introduced.\nThe final handoff requires all eleven checks to pass on the current PR head.\n\nThe five-axis code review found a missing movement offset/limit and late-response/locale review\ninvalidation risks. Regression coverage now enforces exact history pages, unchanged quantities across\nlanguage changes, immutable ambiguous retries and no unsolicited navigation after a delayed response.\nAn intentionally inverted stock-versus-purchase classification fails the new regression; the original\ncode was restored before all client checks. Fmt/Clippy findings were fixed, not suppressed.\n\n## Native browser acceptance\n\nEnvironment: existing Nextcloud **35.0.2**, `AppAPI` **35.0.0**, Chromium, actual authenticated embedded\nroutes/proxy and native assets. Five new scenarios pass against the implementation in this environment:\n\n1. Exact stock, shopping reservation, completed cooking, physical consumption and reversal.\n2. Lost successful response, frozen values, identical retry, one movement and delayed navigation guard.\n3. DE/EN price input, offer review/add, exact package multiplication, purchase booking and reversal.\n4. An actually invited/accepted reader sees stock but no mutation actions; direct writes are denied.\n5. A real second-tab conflict retains the draft, latest-state reload/review, zero correction and archive.\n\nStock, reservation review, offer review and movement history are checked in EN/DE, system light/dark,\nreduced motion and **1440/390/320 px**. Axe WCAG 2/2.1/2.2 A/AA reports zero violations; no horizontal\nworkspace overflow is accepted. Screenshots under ignored `test-results/inventory-*.png` were visually\ninspected for alignment, labels, exact quantities, native contrast and density. This is automated and\nvisual evidence, not formal accessibility certification. Early harness iterations were corrected to\nawait confirmed membership/purchase changes and retain the existing ungrouped exact-quantity format;\nthe completed suite passes without relaxing its functional or accessibility assertions.\n\n## Installed verification and cleanup\n\nThe installed implementation image is\n`sha256:15b52166d8cd7e4bf1b604b48295e9ee249f58018da6c4d07d114e92d91ec20e`.\nPublic JS/CSS served by the `ExApp` match the container assets byte-for-byte and health is verified.\nThe final image passes both isolated **rootless TCP and Unix-socket** smoke transports, including\npreview-without-write, exact stock booking, identical retry, denied foreign-account writes and 0600\nstorage alongside existing authentication, CSRF, shopping, products, cooking, sharing, history, MCP\nand recipe import. The image contains the final runtime implementation; evidence-only documentation\nupdates do not claim a second runtime change.\n\nAll **36/36 distinct installed browser scenarios** passed in final batches of **16/16**, **12/12** and\n**8/8**, covering the 31 existing scenarios and five new F15 scenarios. No final-batch failure was\nwaived. The five new scenarios also passed earlier against the local implementation through the\nreal Nextcloud proxy. Tests run without competing image/Cargo builds.\n\nMain advanced during acceptance with the already customer-merged Node build-image and Vue-Vite-plugin\nupdates (PRs 33/34, main `6709ccf`). An ordinary merge incorporated them; clean npm installation,\n33 client tests, strict production build and both rootless transports passed again. The rebuilt\nimage retained the exact same ID; independent hashes of its public server binary, JS and CSS were\nbyte-identical to those used for the earlier installed batches. No retained data was hashed.\n\nAn additional ledger-owned synthetic household verifies actual installed restart: original exact\n`0.100001 kg`, one opening movement, a dated source allocation and reduced proposed purchase survive.\nReplaying both original requests returns the same operations without duplication, even with their\nold expected revisions. Purchase quantity remains zero. The private snapshot has mode 0600. Normal\nDocker health and asset identity are rechecked after restart; the harness waits for the regular health\nprobe to leave its initial starting state rather than treating an immediate probe race as a failure.\n\nFinal cleanup reports **zero active ledger-owned test households** and the expected image is restarted.\nOnly ledger-owned synthetic households are used. Cleanup stops the sole writer and validates fixture\nidentity/content before archiving its folders and removing its membership/library entries. Every\nnon-ledger household directory remains uninspected, uncopied and unhashed; all retained membership/\nlibrary records and allocation counters are preserved. No reset or old private backup is used.\n"]
