#[doc = "# F16 delivery plan\n\n1. Safe public retrieval and structured extraction: limits/DNS/robots/redirect tests before UI wiring.\n2. Actor-bound previews and immutable reviewed import receipts: canonical publication, provenance,\n   idempotency/body conflicts, current household roles and source-only downstream projection tests.\n3. Native source entry/manual recovery and existing editor review; keyed contracts and draft protection.\n4. Real public-source/manual/SSRF browser checks, rootless transports, installed restart and own-fixture\n   cleanup; required gates and one PR with exact-head CI.\n\n- [x] Read requirements, F16 and existing recipe/quantity/provenance/authentication boundaries.\n- [x] Record threat model, contract, native UX and dependency rationale in ADR 0023.\n- [x] Implement/test bounded fetching and extraction (AC 1, 4, 5).\n- [x] Implement/test canonical reviewed publication and persistent source restrictions (AC 2, 3).\n- [x] Deliver/test the native complete review and manual fallback (AC 1, 2, 5).\n- [x] Verify real installation/restart, all gates and final CI; record evidence and cleanup (AC 1–5).\n\nSee [validation evidence](../page_specs_0016_recipe_import_validation_md/index.html) for acceptance mapping, the installed image, all 31 native\nbrowser scenarios, restart/cleanup and exact current-head PR checks.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0016_recipe_import_plan_md {}

#[doc = "# Customer-operated recipe link import\n\nStatus: Done\nPriority: Should\nOrigin: Customer\nMilestone: M3\n\n## User value\nKeep recipes from source websites in a private recipe library.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. Given a customer-supplied URL (e.g. Chefkoch, Instagram, Einfach Backen), an available importer extracts a preview or clearly reports unsupported/blocked content.\n2. Given an import preview, the customer reviews ingredient mapping, units, steps and provenance before saving; missing fields remain marked unknown.\n3. Given any imported recipe, its original URL and imported-content status persist through revisions, exports and collections; sharing is restricted to the source link.\n4. Given an untrusted URL, fetching rejects private/local addresses, unsafe redirects and excessive responses and does not execute supplied scripts.\n5. Given source restrictions or required login, import does not bypass access controls; manual private entry remains available.\n\n## Out of scope\nGuaranteed support for every website or publication rights obtained merely by importing.\n\n## UX notes\nSee [ux-notes.md](../page_specs_0016_recipe_import_ux_notes_md/index.html) for native review order, unknown fields, draft recovery,\naccessibility and responsive acceptance.\n\n## Links\nRequirement: [F16](../page_docs_requirements_md/index.html). Delivery tasks: [plan.md](../page_specs_0016_recipe_import_plan_md/index.html). Decisions: [adrs.md](../page_specs_0016_recipe_import_adrs_md/index.html).\n\n## Nextcloud delivery contract\nDelivery targets the existing authenticated Nextcloud household editor. These boundaries define\nsupported public retrieval and reviewed manual fallback for all five acceptance criteria.\n\n- Existing owner/editor household authorization protects fetch and save; readers cannot initiate either.\n  Require explicit outbound consent for each URL fetch and retain original requested HTTPS URL across\n  redirects. Manual entry issues no remote request. No login cookies, account headers, referrers,\n  system proxies, script/browser execution or automatic asset/context retrieval.\n- Public HTTPS on port 443 only. Resolve all addresses (maximum 32), reject mixed/public-private sets,\n  special-use, local, mapped/transitional and reserved ranges. Pin accepted addresses in the transport\n  and verify the peer. Validate each of at most three redirect targets before contacting it; reject\n  robots redirects rather than relaxing policy. Respect robots disallow and explicit paywall metadata.\n- Bound total fetch to 15 seconds, page to 2 MiB, robots to 512 KiB and extracted preview/source to\n  96 KiB; accept UTF-8 HTML/JSON-LD (including text/plain carriers) only. At most four simultaneous fetches per\n  process, one per household/account pair and a ten-second pair cooldown in the existing single-writer deployment. No background crawling.\n- Extract up to 16 Schema.org Recipe JSON-LD candidates with original text, author/language, yield,\n  ingredients, steps/sections and optional source durations. Unsupported/login/policy/large/timeout\n  states are actionable and always offer manual private entry. No universal website support claim.\n- Review in the existing compact editor: explicit ingredient IDs, exact quantities and source text per\n  line; inline ingredient creation and normal composition editing remain available. Unrecognized units,\n  ranges, fractions and missing fields stay unknown until explicitly entered. Suggestions never use\n  fuzzy food matching, volume-to-mass assumptions, source health claims or automatic translation.\n- Required canonical values must be supplied; explicit confirmation reviews mapping, servings, steps,\n  source differences and entered time estimates. Original unknown fields remain unknown in retained\n  provenance. External images are not fetched/hotlinked; normal user image upload remains available.\n- Actor-bound previews expire after 30 monotonic minutes, with at most 16 per household and four per\n  account and cleanup within a further 30 seconds. Draft/permission/error/expiry states retain local\n  input until an explicit discard/reload. Confirmed retry uses the same immutable request body/key.\n- Persist selected bounded source fields, importer version, original/final URL, retrieval time and\n  authenticated creation actor/time in the first immutable record, alongside its idempotency receipt.\n  Same request survives retry/concurrency/restart without duplication; changed body/key reuse conflicts.\n  Never store whole HTML. Existing origin rules prevent source removal/change; private reads expose\n  original source fields, while sharing/collections/MCP expose only the retained source URL.\n\n## Acceptance evidence\n[Validation evidence](../page_specs_0016_recipe_import_validation_md/index.html) maps parser/transport/permission/review/atomic-retry regressions,\n31 installed native browser scenarios, rootless transports and an actual installed restart to AC 1–5.\nRequired gates and current-head CI accompany [PR #35](https://github.com/Th3Link/mealshop/pull/35).\nOnly ledger-owned synthetic households were inspected/archived; retained directories were not read.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0016_recipe_import_specification_md {}

#[doc = "# Review a source before adding it to your household\n\nUse the existing Nextcloud recipe header and add Import from link beside Create recipe. The first\nview asks for the source URL and explicit permission to contact its public host/validated redirects.\nExplain server-IP/link disclosure and that access restrictions will not be bypassed. Manual entry is\nalways available. Loading disables repeated requests; errors have a specific reason and next action.\n\nShow multiple extracted recipes in a labelled selector. Continue into the existing always-open compact\nrecipe editor. Keep original ingredient text beside its mapping/quantity, show known/unknown source\nyield/times and keep external text plain. Required missing values block save. Inline ingredient\ncreation stays in context. A review checkbox starts unchecked and changes invalidate confirmation.\nNo source nutrition/diet claim is promoted to a catalogue fact. Native image upload is explicit.\n\nKeep the original URL fixed. Saved details show provenance and original fields separately from the\nreviewed recipe. Conflicting/expired/unauthorized saves retain the draft; an ambiguous submission is\nfrozen and retries the same body/key. Leaving/replacing input requires explicit discard. No source\ncontent goes into browser storage. Source links are explicit actions, never automatic requests.\n\nUse native components, theme tokens, EN/DE keys, ordinary type and compact spacing. UX/UI Pro Max\ninforms review order and recovery, Taste informs alignment and consistency; Nextcloud rules always\nwin. Verify keyboard/focus, 1440/390/320 px, themes, axe, real proxy routes and zero page errors.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0016_recipe_import_ux_notes_md {}

#[doc = "# F16 validation evidence\n\nDate: 2026-11-12. The implementation and current-head CI are attached to\n[PR #35](https://github.com/Th3Link/mealshop/pull/35). The delivery contract covers public structured\nextraction and explicit private review, with manual entry for unavailable or unsupported sources.\nIt does not claim universal website support, login bypass or publication rights.\n\n## Acceptance trace\n\n| Criterion | Evidence |\n| --- | --- |\n| AC 1: URL preview or actionable unsupported/blocked result | `src/imports/parser_tests.rs`, `src/imports/network_tests.rs`, real public HTTPS fixture retrieval and native multi-candidate/manual controls. HTML, JSON-LD arrays/graphs and nested instruction sections are supported. |\n| AC 2: explicit ingredient/quantity/step/provenance review; unknown originals | `tests/recipe_import.rs`, `src/imports/receipt_tests.rs`, Vue quantity/draft contracts and native browser review. No identity guessing, translation, implicit volume conversion or source nutrition/diet adoption. Missing required canonical values prevent save. |\n| AC 3: persistent source restrictions | First-revision source receipt reload/edit/historical tests; `src/exapp/import_tests.rs` checks recipient source-only projection. Existing sharing/collection/MCP regressions remain required. |\n| AC 4: hostile network/content boundary | DNS mixture/rebinding, private/special address families, alternate IP encodings, unsafe redirects, robots, size/type limits and non-executing parser checks. The browser fixture contains script/image sentinels that must never load. |\n| AC 5: access restrictions and manual fallback | Robots and explicit paywall checks fail closed. Reader and foreign-account restrictions are covered at HTTP and trusted Nextcloud boundaries; manual entry makes no network request. |\n\nThe 12 new Rust regressions comprise three network-policy tests, three parser tests, two source\nreceipt tests, three HTTP import tests and one trusted Nextcloud adapter test. Concurrent identical\nrequests publish one recipe; changed payload/key reuse conflicts. The receipt and selected source\nfields are atomically published with revision one, survive actual storage reopen and retain private\n0600 permissions. Receipt keys and preview IDs do not appear in public recipe projections.\n\n## Local gates and container compatibility\n\nThe complete local gate passed:\n\n- Catalogue import/check and verifier; nutrition-estimate import/check and verifier; conversion and\n  allergen verification; demo syntax and keyed i18n tests.\n- `cargo fmt --all --check`, Clippy with warnings denied, **154/154** nextest tests, unchanged licence\n  policy, advisory audit and strict rustdoc. Existing dependency versions remain pinned; the new\n  HTML5 tokenizer and robots matcher add no browser runtime or advisory exception.\n- Native Prettier, strict Vue/TypeScript and Vite build; **32/32** Vitest contracts; npm audit with\n  zero vulnerabilities; generated MCP schema verification; **5/5** Python bridge tests and official\n  SDK modern HTTP and auto/legacy/pinned-modern stdio interoperability.\n- `cargo +1.85.0 check --workspace --all-targets --locked` passes; the pinned container compiler\n  is verified directly as **1.99.1**. The final rootless image passes isolated **TCP and Unix-socket**\n  smoke tests, including manual import, unsafe-target rejection, explicit review, identical retry,\n  reader denial and private first-revision storage alongside existing domain and MCP flows.\n\nThe final handoff requires all eleven CI checks to pass on the current PR head. The PR Checks tab\nis the authoritative current-head record; no failing check is waived.\n\n## Native browser evidence\n\nEnvironment: existing Nextcloud **35.0.2**, `AppAPI` **35.0.0**, Chromium, authenticated embedded routes\nand the actual proxy. Three new import scenarios passed against the implementation using its native\nassets; all three also passed against the installed image. A real public HTTPS request retrieves\nthe committed synthetic fixture; transport is not mocked. Before merge, `MEALSHOP_IMPORT_FIXTURE_URL` points to the immutable implementation commit;\nthe default points to the versioned fixture on main after merge.\n\nThe import scenarios cover consent, preserved exact `100.500000 g` input, explicit ingredient IDs,\noriginal versus revised source fields, source-only sharing notice, rejected unsafe URLs, manual\nfallback, required missing values, lost successful-response retry without duplication, explicit\ndiscard and an actual accepted reader's hidden/disabled/denied import operations. Source script,\nimage and health-claim sentinels are never executed, loaded or promoted into recipe nutrition.\n\nEN/DE, system light/dark, reduced motion, keyboard and **1440/390/320 px** review views pass axe\nWCAG 2/2.1/2.2 A/AA with zero reported violations and no horizontal page overflow or page errors.\nScreenshots were visually inspected. This is automated/visual evidence, not formal certification.\nThe saved source text remains separate from reviewed ingredient mappings and quantities.\n\nA deliberately delayed retry response reproduced an unsolicited redirect after the user confirmed\nleaving the import. The import now captures its view generation/destination and ignores responses\nafter navigation or unmount. The retry regression requires the recipe list to remain open with\nexactly one imported recipe after the held response arrives.\n\nAll **31/31 distinct embedded browser scenarios** have passed against the final installed image\nacross batches. The first implementation image also passed the complete **28/28** existing suite in\none invocation. The final navigation-guard image passed the three import scenarios **3/3**.\n\nIts repeated baseline invocation passed 24 scenarios, failed two and did not run two serial dependants:\na native navigation click stalled after scrolling, before reaching the meal-plan view. That setup had\nnot created the meal required by a later usability scenario. The trace showed successful fixture API\nresponses and no application console errors; the failed action could not capture a final screenshot.\nThe underlying cause of that one click stall was not established. After synthetic cleanup, the entire\nNextcloud/usability block passed **6/6**, including every initially failed/skipped scenario, with fresh\nfixtures, no parallel local builds and unchanged assertions/timeouts. No persistent product failure\nwas reproduced or failing scenario waived.\n\nSynthetic cleanup between batches respects the existing 20-household account limit. No capacity,\nassertion or timeout was relaxed, and no concurrent manual fixture was created.\n\n## Installation, restart and cleanup\n\nInstalled implementation image:\n`sha256:4f51e81eba963f7b078aa3682339d0230cb004b66140fdf5cc095eada192464a`\n(`mealshop.local/mealshop:reviewed-recipe-import`). Public JavaScript (**1,510,135 bytes**) and CSS\n(**169,350 bytes**) match the installed container asset hashes. The implementation image is healthy;\nthe image contains the final behavior, including the navigation guard. Subsequent changes update\ndocumentation only.\n\nAn actual container restart in a newly recorded synthetic household retained the fetched source\nsnapshot and atomic import receipt. An identical confirmed retry returned the same first revision,\nincluding after a normal edit; there was exactly one recipe. Uncommitted previews disappeared on\nrestart, later edits retained original source fields and a pinned MCP read remained source-link-only.\n\nWith the sole writer stopped, cleanup validated and privately archived only newly ledger-recorded\nsynthetic households. Every non-fixture membership/library entry and allocation counter was\npreserved; retained household directories were never inspected, hashed or copied. The final ledger\ncheck reports **zero active synthetic households** and the cleaned installed image is healthy.\nNo reset or retained recipe inspection was performed. `AGENTS.md` is unchanged.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0016_recipe_import_validation_md {}

