#[doc = "# F17 delivery plan\n\n1. Canonical creation preview and atomic recipe receipt: model → file publication → retry/restart tests.\n2. Disabled-by-default account scopes and bounded MCP protocol/tools: current membership → canonical\n   recipe/ingredient adapters → source-only projection → permission/protocol tests.\n3. Stdio connection and native setup/activity: credential handling → explicit grants → user flows.\n4. Real Nextcloud/client/container verification, synthetic cleanup, full gates and one reviewable PR.\n\n## Tasks\n- [x] Read requirements/F17 and current source, quantity, recipe and authorization boundaries.\n- [x] Record delivery contract, trust boundaries, native UX and primary protocol sources before code.\n- [x] Implement canonical nonpersistent validation and atomic audited/idempotent creation.\n- [x] Implement owner-managed scopes, current-role enforcement and bounded dual-era MCP tools.\n- [x] Ship stdio bridge and native setup/activity with safe credentials and explicit confirmation.\n- [x] Verify all acceptance criteria, browser/client/container/restart and cleanup; record evidence.\n- [x] Run required gates and prepare one PR; verify exact-head remote CI before handoff.\n\nAC 1: authenticated discovery/search/read/preview and real client flow.\nAC 2: canonical validation parity, provenance restrictions and immutable creation audit.\nAC 3: current role, explicit scope, revocation and household isolation tests.\nAC 4: identical/concurrent/restarted retries, conflicting reuse and structured quantity errors.\n\n## Delivery evidence\n\nSee [validation.md](../page_specs_0017_mcp_validation_md/index.html) for the 142-test backend gate, real official-client/Nextcloud\nconnection, all 28 distinct browser scenarios across batches, installed restart and synthetic-only\ncleanup. [PR #32](https://github.com/Th3Link/mealshop/pull/32) carries the final-head CI checks.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0017_mcp_plan_md {}

#[doc = "# MCP recipe tools\n\nStatus: Done\nPriority: Should\nOrigin: Customer\nMilestone: M3\n\n## User value\nManage recipes through authorized assistant tooling.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. Given an authenticated MCP client, scoped tools search/read authorized recipes and preview insertion of a structured recipe.\n2. Given recipe creation, validation and imported-content sharing restrictions match the regular API and the action is auditable.\n3. Given a household boundary or read-only scope, tools cannot expose another household or mutate data.\n4. Given repeated insertion with an idempotency key, the server avoids duplicate recipes and returns a structured error for invalid quantities.\n\n## Out of scope\nUnauthenticated access or treating imported recipe text as tool instructions.\n\n## UX notes\nUI flows, accessibility, empty/error states and user review points must be specified before Ready.\n\n## Links\nRequirement: [F17](../page_docs_requirements_md/index.html). Delivery tasks: [plan.md](../page_specs_0017_mcp_plan_md/index.html). Decisions: [adrs.md](../page_specs_0017_mcp_adrs_md/index.html).\n\n## Nextcloud delivery contract\nThe customer requests F17 after merging F11. Under the standing autonomous-work instruction this\ncontract moves through Ready into In progress before implementation. No cloud AI provider, OAuth\nserver, account system or mandatory SDK/runtime dependency is introduced.\n\n- Reuse the authenticated Nextcloud `AppAPI` proxy and current household membership on every request.\n  A household owner explicitly grants each existing account Disabled, Read or Read/create MCP scope;\n  default is Disabled. The effective capability is the intersection of that grant and current role.\n  Readers never create recipes. Changing/removing access invalidates subsequent calls and previews.\n  A grant conveys no access to another household, profiles, plans, shopping or learning data.\n- Offer a bounded stateless JSON-RPC MCP endpoint under the existing household domain. Support current\n  MCP 2026-07-28 metadata/discovery and legacy 2025-11-25 initialization for existing clients. Use JSON\n  responses; no SSE subscriptions, sampling, remote fetches or notifications are advertised. Reject\n  browser Origin headers on the RPC transport; native setup uses ordinary protected REST instead.\n  Preserve the existing write marker, JSON limits, enabled-state checks and no-store responses.\n- Supply a stdio bridge using Python's standard library and environment-provided Nextcloud username,\n  app password and exact MCP URL. Credentials never enter JSON-RPC results, command arguments, logs\n  or browser storage. Require HTTPS except explicitly local loopback development; reject redirects.\n  App passwords retain their underlying Nextcloud account authority; they are not household-limited\n  OAuth tokens. For an untrusted client use a dedicated least-privilege account. Hosted OAuth and\n  independently delegated per-client credentials remain outside this existing Nextcloud slice.\n- Discover/search ingredients by stable IDs and localized aliases; search/read owned recipes in the\n  selected household with bounded pages and pinned revisions. Imported recipes, including older\n  revisions subsequently marked imported, expose only their retained original HTTPS source URL.\n  Do not search imported title/body/nutrition or export their text, ingredients, steps or images.\n  Content is untrusted data and never changes the tool allowlist, identity or operation semantics.\n- Preview a structured recipe through canonical recipe, ingredient, exact quantity, composition,\n  provenance and image validation. Preview is nonpersistent and bound to actor, current scope and\n  ingredient revision, expires after ten minutes, and cannot create a recipe. Imported preview\n  results remain source-only. No allergy safety, density or nutritional value is inferred.\n- Creation requires the actor's still-valid preview, explicit client confirmation and an opaque\n  idempotency key. Confirmation is a client attestation, not proof of physical human review; hosts\n  must allow users to deny writes. Invalid quantities return structured tool errors. An old preview\n  after changed ingredients requires a new preview. Unknown fields cannot select another household.\n- Persist creation actor/time, preview identity and idempotency receipt atomically inside the first\n  immutable recipe revision. The canonical append-only recipe transaction is the sole publication\n  point. Same actor/key/preview returns the original reference across retries, concurrency and restart;\n  the same key with another preview is a conflict. Do not use a separate journal that can drift from\n  recipe publication. Later edits retain the receipt in revision one and current imported restrictions.\n- Native setup shows the current scope, exact proxy URL, credential-free connection example and\n  household-visible creation audit with pinned recipe links. Only the owner edits grants; readers\n  see their scope and activity. Explain export/confirmation and unknowns before connection.\n\n## Verification\nTrace the four acceptance criteria to protocol, canonical validation, current-role/scope, source-only\nhistorical reads, concurrent/restarted idempotency and malformed input regressions. Exercise a real MCP\nclient plus the stdio bridge, real Nextcloud account authentication, native EN/DE themes/responsiveness,\nall required repository/client/container gates and exact-head PR CI. Live checks use only new ledger-\nrecorded synthetic households; do not inspect or copy retained household directories.\n\nAcceptance evidence: [validation.md](../page_specs_0017_mcp_validation_md/index.html). Hosted OAuth, independently delegated credentials\nand model-provider configuration are not part of the accepted Nextcloud tool contract.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0017_mcp_specification_md {}

#[doc = "# Native assistant connection and recipe receipts\n\nUse a household Assistant tools view with the existing Nextcloud page header and ordinary labelled\ncontrols. Show the current user's effective scope first, then the copyable exact endpoint and a\ncredential-free stdio example. Explain that recipe content is sent to the configured assistant,\nimported recipes remain source-only, and creation needs a preview plus explicit host confirmation.\nNever display/store app passwords or the `ExApp` service secret.\n\nAn owner sees current member IDs/roles and a Disabled/Read/Read and create selector per account.\nReader rows cannot select creation. Save/reload use a revision and retain conflicting drafts; changes\nare protected when navigating away. Non-owners see their own scope, not editable owner controls.\nAudit rows show actor/time and pinned recipe references, without idempotency keys or recipe contents.\nRemoved/unavailable references and loading/empty/error/revocation states stay explicit.\n\nUse keyed EN/DE messages, native Vue controls, theme tokens and focus feedback. Taste governs\nalignment/spacing and UI/UX Pro Max guides setup clarity; do not add marketing assets, palettes,\nfonts or a new design system. Verify keyboard, 1440/390/320 px, light/dark, axe and real Nextcloud.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0017_mcp_ux_notes_md {}

#[doc = "# F17 validation evidence\n\nDate: 2026-11-12. Implementation: `d6788cc`; final-head checks are attached to\n[PR #32](https://github.com/Th3Link/mealshop/pull/32). F17 is complete for the documented Nextcloud\ncontract; no OAuth provider or independently delegated per-client credential is claimed.\n\n## Acceptance trace\n\n| Criterion | Evidence |\n| --- | --- |\n| AC 1: authenticated scoped discovery/read/preview | `tests/mcp.rs`, official SDK 2.4.0 modern direct HTTP and auto/legacy/pinned-modern stdio, and real Nextcloud native connection. |\n| AC 2: canonical validation, provenance and audit | `src/recipe_creation_tests.rs`, canonical quantity/image/ingredient/composition validation, source-only retroactive historical reads, private first-revision actor/time and native pinned activity links. |\n| AC 3: role/scope and household boundaries | `src/exapp/mcp_tests.rs`, disabled/read/create grants, current role intersection/removal, reader create denial, foreign-account/home denial and immediate MCP grant revocation. |\n| AC 4: idempotency and structured quantity errors | concurrent HTTP insert/restart/key-conflict tests, official SDK retry identity and an actual installed container restart preserving one recipe and receipt. |\n\nThe 16 new Rust regressions comprise nine HTTP/protocol tests, two trusted Nextcloud adapter tests,\nthree canonical receipt tests and two settings/preview-lifetime tests. They cover malformed/oversized\nRPC, metadata/header disagreements, Origin rejection, legacy missing params, exact quantity-only\ninput, no-write preview/denied confirmation, changed ingredients/grants, monotonic expiry, corrupt or\nduplicate receipts and private 0600 settings/recipe files. A reproduced failed scope-revocation write\npreviously left stale capabilities usable; its regression now verifies that all tools and scope reads\nreturn unavailable until recovery, with no recipe inserted.\n\n## Local and independent-client gates\n\nPassed:\n\n- Catalogue import/check and verifier; nutrition-estimate import/check and verifier; conversion and\n  allergen verification; demo syntax and keyed i18n tests.\n- `cargo fmt --all --check`, Clippy with warnings denied, **142/142** nextest tests, licence policy,\n  advisory audit and strict rustdoc. No runtime crate or advisory exception was added.\n- Native Prettier, strict Vue/TypeScript and Vite build; **30/30** Vitest contracts; npm audit with\n  zero vulnerabilities; generated MCP JSON schema checked against committed recipe contracts.\n- **5/5** Python standard-library bridge tests: protected configuration, mirrored protocol headers,\n  bounded input, redirect rejection and sanitized/unmatched upstream responses.\n- Official SDK **2.4.0**: modern HTTP and auto/legacy/pinned-modern stdio interoperate with the actual\n  Rust binary; exact quantities, preview/confirmation, repeated creation, private audit, historical\n  source-only projection and scope reduction are asserted using isolated synthetic state.\n- Final Rust-1.85 `ExApp` image passes the isolated rootless **TCP and Unix-socket** smoke suite,\n  including existing shopping/cooking/sharing/history flows and MCP preview/create/retry/redaction.\n\nCI includes an independent official-client/stdio job against its compiled debug artifact. The final\nhandoff requires all eleven checks to pass on the current PR head. The PR Checks tab is the\nauthoritative current-head record.\n\n## Real Nextcloud and browser checks\n\nEnvironment: existing Nextcloud **35.0.2**, `AppAPI` **35.0.0**, Chromium, native embedded routing and the\nreal authenticated proxy. The official SDK/stdio browser flow authenticates as the real owner and\naccepted reader, creates from a quantity-only preview, retries after client restart, follows the\npinned audit link and proves that a subsequent imported restriction hides revision one's contents.\nOwner reduction/revocation applies on subsequent calls. A second browser scenario verifies two-tab\nconflict retention and explicit navigation/reload discard decisions.\n\nEN/DE, system light/dark, reduced motion, keyboard and **1440/390/320 px** are covered. Axe WCAG\n2/2.1/2.2 A/AA checks report zero violations in both owner and reader views at these sizes. Header,\nconnection and activity screenshots were inspected; no horizontal page overflow or page errors occurred.\nThis is automated/visual evidence, not a claim of formal accessibility certification.\n\nAll **28 distinct embedded browser scenarios** have passed across batches. The first complete\ninvocation passed 26 and hit the existing account household limit in unified preparation and visual\nshopping: two additional manual app-password fixture households were created concurrently. After\narchiving only owned fixtures, the permission-guard image passed **4/4** targeted cases: both MCP\nscenarios plus both capacity-blocked scenarios. After adding exact source-portion discovery, the final\nimage passed both MCP scenarios again; the native application assets are unchanged. No product capacity was relaxed and no failing behavior was skipped.\nFuture full runs must start with fixture capacity available and avoid concurrent manual fixture creation.\n\nA separate short-lived, uniquely named **actual Nextcloud app password** authenticated stdio discovery\nthrough the real proxy. Only that test token was deleted. Its next calls were denied after the installed\nNextcloud authentication cache expired (**11.3 s observed**; installed provider TTL is 10 s). This\nupstream cache is distinct from Mealshop's immediate per-call MCP grant/role checks. Credentials stayed\nin process memory/environment and were never copied to a file or tool output.\n\n## Installed restart and cleanup\n\nFinal installed image:\n`sha256:ff307fe41d3d0ffc2ee6bbdcbbf305d9c32b3ff629701f44cbe3f218c6edbcb1`\n(`mealshop.local/mealshop:mcp-recipe-tools`). It is healthy. Public JavaScript (**1,490,474 bytes**) and\nCSS (**168,690 bytes**) match the image's asset hashes; the development SDK is outside the browser graph.\nThe image contains the verified implementation; subsequent changes are documentation and screenshot\ncoverage only.\n\nAn actual container restart in a newly ledger-recorded fixture retained its account grant and exact\nfirst-revision creation receipt/audit. A retry returned that same revision, stayed source-only after a\nlater imported edit, and left exactly one recipe. The uncommitted preview disappeared on restart;\nreducing scope then denied even a completed-write retry.\n\nExact source-portion discovery is additionally tested through the real proxy; custom food records\ndo not receive a neighbouring reference conversion.\n\nAll created browser/manual/restart households are privately ledger-recorded. With the sole writer\nstopped, cleanup validates only those synthetic directories and archives them. All non-fixture\nmembership/library entries and allocation counters are preserved; retained household directories are\nnot inspected, hashed or copied. No test app password remains. The final fixture check reports zero active ledger households, and the cleaned installed container\nis healthy.\nAGENTS.md is unchanged.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0017_mcp_validation_md {}

