#[doc = "# Plan for Storage adapters, Nextcloud `ExApp` and Flutter\n\n## Affected modules\n`src/recipes.rs` and `src/recipe_api.rs` begin a bounded local file slice alongside F04.\nNo generic repository trait, SQL/Git adapter or placeholder crate is added.\n\n## Tasks\n- [ ] Design and implement the behaviour for AC 1; add acceptance evidence.\n- [ ] Design and implement the behaviour for AC 2; add acceptance evidence.\n- [ ] Design and implement the behaviour for AC 3; add acceptance evidence.\n- [ ] Design and implement the behaviour for AC 4; add acceptance evidence.\n- [ ] Design and implement the behaviour for AC 5; add acceptance evidence.\n\n## Validation\nBefore implementation, derive acceptance tests from each numbered criterion. Include failure cases, household authorization and quantity/provenance checks where applicable. Record commands and results here at delivery.\n\nProduct web UI coordination: F22/F30; cross-client localization: F21/F29. The existing demo is not deployment UI.\n\nCurrent local part of AC 5: exclusive lock, immutable revisions, expected-revision conflicts,\nfail-closed startup and documented backup/recovery (ADR 0009). Tests in `tests/recipes.rs`\nexercise these behaviours. This does not complete any full multi-adapter/client criterion.\n\n## Flutter coordination (planned, 2026-11-13)\n\n[F35](../page_specs_0035_flutter_mobile_client_specification_md/index.html) and its\n[five-PR phone plan](../page_specs_0035_flutter_mobile_client_plan_md/index.html) own the mobile delivery backlog, including\nAC4's endpoint configuration/failure UX. This planning change does not complete AC4 or the remaining\nstorage/standalone contracts above. No existing unchecked task is removed or marked implemented.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0018_storage_deployment_plan_md {}

#[doc = "# Storage adapters, Nextcloud `ExApp` and Flutter\n\nStatus: In progress\nPriority: Must\nOrigin: Customer\nMilestone: M1\n\n## User value\nUse an own server or the hosted service without locking household data to one backend.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. Given a deployment, one selected backend persists equivalent versioned records using Git-backed files, SQLite, PostgreSQL or MariaDB.\n2. Given a backend migration, an export/import round trip preserves identities, quantities, permissions, provenance and relationships and is verified before switching.\n3. Given a Nextcloud `ExApp` installation, the Axum service integrates with supported `AppAPI` lifecycle/authentication; installation remains free.\n4. Given a Flutter app, users can configure an own server or hosted endpoint and understand connection/authentication failures.\n5. Given concurrent edits or a Git conflict, data is not silently overwritten; recovery and backup/restore behaviour is documented per adapter.\n\n6. Nextcloud and standalone product web shells follow F22/F30 (Vue 3); the current nutrition\n   browser demo does not satisfy product integration. Localization follows F21; Flutter remains distinct.\n\n## Current slice\nF04 starts one local file store with immutable schema-1 revisions and pinned catalogue inputs.\nIt is not Git-backed and does not complete AC 1. Dedicated-directory exclusive locking,\nexpected-revision writes and fail-closed recovery address a bounded local part of AC 5.\nSee [ADR 0009](../page_docs_adr_0009_local_recipe_revisions_md/index.html) and the\n[operator guide](../page_docs_guides_recipes_md/index.html). SQL/Git adapters, migration and Flutter remain unimplemented. The customer-authorized\nNextcloud slice now adds authenticated `AppAPI` lifecycle/transport, shared-household roles and\nprivate file stores; real-host and container deployment evidence are\ntracked in [F22](../page_specs_0022_product_web_clients_plan_md/index.html) and the [Nextcloud guide](../page_docs_guides_nextcloud_md/index.html).\n\n## Out of scope\nAll adapters in the bootstrap, an unvalidated common SQL dialect or a prematurely selected sync algorithm.\n\n## UX notes\nUI flows, accessibility, empty/error states and user review points must be specified before Ready.\n\n## Links\nRequirement: [F18](../page_docs_requirements_md/index.html). Delivery tasks: [plan.md](../page_specs_0018_storage_deployment_plan_md/index.html). Decisions: [adrs.md](../page_specs_0018_storage_deployment_adrs_md/index.html).\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0018_storage_deployment_specification_md {}

