#[doc = "# Federated recipe and meal-plan exchange\n\nStatus: Draft\nPriority: Could\nOrigin: Customer\nMilestone: M5\n\n## User value\nExchange selected content between independent Mealshop servers.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. Given opt-in federation, a user can share an authorized recipe between servers without opening private household data.\n2. Given a shared meal-plan template for similar intolerances, sharing uses explicit consent and minimal disclosed attributes, never raw health profiles by default.\n3. Given imported recipes, the exchanged representation contains the original source link only.\n4. Given an untrusted remote server, authentication, protocol versioning, moderation, revocation limitations and abuse controls are specified and tested before enablement.\n\n## Out of scope\nA federation protocol choice or automatic cross-server health-profile discovery.\n\n## UX notes\nUI flows, accessibility, empty/error states and user review points must be specified before Ready.\n\n## Links\nRequirement: [F20](../page_docs_requirements_md/index.html). Delivery tasks: [plan.md](../page_specs_0020_federation_plan_md/index.html). Decisions: [adrs.md](../page_specs_0020_federation_adrs_md/index.html).\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0020_federation_specification_md {}

#[doc = "# Decisions for internationalization\n\n- [ADR 0007](../page_docs_adr_0007_localization_and_web_clients_md/index.html): de/en first; demo vs product boundary.\n- [ADR 0002](../page_docs_adr_0002_quantities_and_nutrition_md/index.html): preserve exact amounts and unit meanings.\n\n## Slice-local proposals\nUse a small framework-free ES module for demo-only resources and pure locale helpers, with\nNode's built-in test runner. No JavaScript dependencies or production i18n framework are chosen.\nScope starter ingredient translations by source record identity, not a possibly colliding\noperator-defined ingredient ID. Untranslated data keeps its source wording and attribution.\nCanonical HTTP decimal strings remain dot-separated; only the presentation boundary uses commas.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0021_internationalization_adrs_md {}

#[doc = "# F21 Nextcloud delivery\n\n- [x] Keyed de/en resources, explicit choice, regional normalization and English fallback.\n- [x] Reviewed localized ingredient names/search, source-language fallback and exact decimal boundaries.\n- [x] Locale switching preserves valid and invalid authoring input; dates/counts/serving plurals use the active locale.\n- [x] Typed API contracts and stable error/warning codes preserve server calculations and original facts.\n- [x] Customer-approved follow-up F29 retains the original full acceptance contract.\n\n## Acceptance evidence\n`node --test tests/i18n.test.mjs` covers the demo baseline. `npm --prefix clients/nextcloud run test`\ncovers native exact boundaries, localized input, regional normalization, serving plurals and date/meal presentation.\nEmbedded Nextcloud E2E contracts cover German entry, switching, fallback labels and quantity persistence.\nSee F06 validation for the final combined run and F22 validation for the previously delivered native shell.\n\nNo standalone or Flutter implementation is claimed.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0021_internationalization_plan_md {}

#[doc = "# Nextcloud internationalization and localized presentation\n\nStatus: Done\nPriority: Must\nOrigin: Customer-approved Nextcloud scope separation, 2026-11-10\nMilestone: M1\n\n## User value\nUse the shipped Nextcloud application in German or English without changing stored quantities or source facts.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. Keyed de/en messages, explicit language choice, regional-tag normalization and English fallback work in the Nextcloud client.\n2. Existing reviewed ingredient translations and aliases support discovery; unavailable recipe/source translations remain visibly original. No generated translation replaces source content.\n3. Exact localized decimal input/output preserves six digits and valid values during locale switches; invalid inputs are never reinterpreted silently.\n4. Dates, integer counts and serving plurals use the active locale independently of units. API identities, units and canonical decimal strings remain stable.\n5. Error and warning presentation uses stable codes and focused UI/API checks; calculations and source provenance remain on the server.\n\n## Scope decision\nThe customer explicitly approved closing the Nextcloud delivery and retaining all unfinished work in separate specifications.\n[F29](../page_specs_0029_cross_client_localization_specification_md/index.html) preserves the original six acceptance criteria verbatim, including\nversioned content translations, API negotiation, complete parameterized backend errors and standalone/Flutter coverage.\nThose requirements remain open; this Done status does not claim their implementation.\n\n## Evidence\nSee [plan.md](../page_specs_0021_internationalization_plan_md/index.html), [F22 validation](../page_specs_0022_product_web_clients_validation_md/index.html),\nand the combined [shopping delivery validation](../page_specs_0006_shopping_list_validation_md/index.html).\n\n## UX\n[ux-notes.md](../page_specs_0021_internationalization_ux_notes_md/index.html). Native host conventions take precedence.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0021_internationalization_specification_md {}

#[doc = "# Demo localization UX\n\n- A visible language selector offers Deutsch and English. Initial preference: saved choice,\n  otherwise the browser language (de variants map to German, unsupported languages to English).\n- All demo controls/statuses have keyed messages. German ingredient names are shown for reviewed\n  starter record identities; custom/unknown records use their original names without guessed translations.\n- Search matches localized labels, canonical names and aliases in both supported languages.\n- German gram input uses a comma, English a dot; no grouping separators are accepted in inputs.\n  Outputs may group digits. Switching language preserves exact values and results; invalid\n  fields keep their text and require correction rather than being reinterpreted in the new locale.\n- Original-language provenance, uncertainty and education are labelled explicitly. Missing\n  translations must not hide limitations or imply content has been reviewed in German.\n- Header/title/footer say Demo; replace marketing copy with a pragmatic explanation. No redesign.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0021_internationalization_ux_notes_md {}

