#[doc = "# Native Nextcloud daily workflows\n\nStatus: Done\nOrigin: Customer, 2026-11-09, after PR #15 merge\n\n## Acceptance contract\n\n1. A persistent native household switcher changes context without visiting household management. Opening the app restores the last accessible household for the current account; explicit household management and deep links remain available. Revoked households never become an authority through saved preferences.\n2. Recipe creation has a plus icon. Author attribution is optional. Exact quantities omit redundant trailing fractional zeros for display, without changing stored input or precision. Recipe images are optional, private to the household and persist across restart.\n3. Recipe ingredient selection supports multilingual search, quick keyboard selection and inline creation without losing the recipe draft. A labelled trash icon ends each ingredient row.\n4. The weekly meal calendar has breakfast, lunch, snack and dinner slots. People may attend or skip each meal independently; serving estimates and shopping changes remain explicit and reviewed. Existing plans remain editable and no calendar provider is implied.\n5. Invitations use native searchable account selection with Nextcloud's actual sharing visibility rules, retaining addressed invitation acceptance and household roles.\n6. Ingredient search retains focus while typing. Household editors can create and archive ingredients; readers cannot mutate shared catalogue data. Bundled primary records are not destroyed. Favourites persist and reverse lookup lists matching saved recipes.\n7. Ingredients support household tags and explicit composition. Ingredient IDs remain language independent. Composition references are validated and cannot cycle. Declared allergen information and nested ingredients participate in conservative hard exclusions; ordinary tags cannot assert allergy safety. Missing composition/nutrition remains unknown.\n8. Existing source snapshots, recipe revisions, health-data isolation, role revocation, exact quantities, host theme and accessible mobile operation remain intact. Backend changes have restart/conflict/permission tests and all new UI paths are exercised in the real test instance.\n\n## Safe implementation decisions\n\nHousehold catalogue additions and annotations are shared within that household only. Removing a referenced ingredient archives it for new selection; existing recipe snapshots remain readable. User declarations are labelled as declarations, never primary nutrient records. Composition membership does not imply a known mass ratio or nutrient composition. No automatic nutritional estimate is made from a composite's name or nearby food.\n\n## Links\nF02/F04/F09/F10/F22 remain the domain contracts. See ux-notes.md, adrs.md and plan.md for this customer-authorized extension.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0024_nextcloud_daily_workflows_specification_md {}

#[doc = "# Daily workflow UX\n\nUse native Nextcloud controls and tokens. Put the household selector at the top of the existing app navigation and keep household management separately reachable. Remember only the account-scoped household ID in browser preferences.\n\nRecipe rows combine searchable ingredient selection, exact quantity/unit and a trailing labelled trash action. Inline ingredient creation is a bounded native dialog that returns the created ingredient into the same row without leaving the recipe draft. Optional attribution and image controls do not block basic recipe creation.\n\nThe calendar exposes a week with four named slots per date. Each slot opens the existing reviewed plan workflow with date/meal prefilled. Attendance is labelled per person, and skipped people are explicit. On narrow screens, days stack rather than making the whole document scroll horizontally.\n\nIngredient management distinguishes reviewed reference data from household declarations. Source records remain immutable; archive and favourites are annotations. Composition, free tags and structured declared allergens are distinct controls. Reverse lookup names recipes and preserves navigation back to the ingredient.\n\nSearch, theme transitions, focus and unsaved-draft handling must be exercised using real Nextcloud DOM and screenshots. No global style reset, font, colour palette or replacement navigation is introduced.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0024_nextcloud_daily_workflows_ux_notes_md {}

#[doc = "# Daily workflow validation\n\nStatus: Done; implemented and verified on the supplied test instance.\n\n- Rust acceptance suite: 49 passed, including optional author/restart, household declarations,\n  composition cycles, isolation, archive, reverse lookup, private raster assets and pinned hard\n  allergen/tag exclusions, concurrent tag/plan application and legacy-overlay loading. New archives are also rejected when introduced through recipe writes.\n- Real JPEG and WebP fixtures additionally passed upload/private byte round trips; PNG, invalid active content, oversized dimensions and immutable references remain covered.\n- Strict client type checking and five unit tests passed. Compact decimal display retains exact\n  numeric value and does not modify source precision or the six-decimal input contract.\n- Real Nextcloud 35.0.2/AppAPI 35.0.0 browser suite: five tests passed together (approximately 1.5 minutes).\n  Existing invitation/reader/revocation/conflict, localized quantities and native themes still pass.\n- The new browser workflow verifies account-scoped default household and switching, focus across\n  every search character, inline composite creation without losing the recipe title, empty author,\n  200 g/400 g display, a valid PNG above 128 KiB through the proxy, image reload, shared favourite,\n  archive/restore, reverse recipe lookup, calendar attendance and hard tag conflicts only for attendees.\n- Browser bounds and automated accessibility are checked at 320/390/768/1440 pixels; native\n  light/dark and reduced-motion checks remain in the suite. Screenshots were inspected and the\n  calendar was refined to align slots and restore focus/week context after editor operations.\n- Two additional daily-workflow tests passed together in 33.5 seconds, including simultaneous\n  ingredient editors: stale writes preserve the draft; explicit reload obtains the saved version.\n\n## Final packaged deployment\n\nThe complete immutable image (2635bf700f9f) is running as UID/GID 1000 with a read-only root\nfilesystem. The temporary development asset mount was removed and its absence inspected.\nAll six browser tests passed together against this package in approximately 1.6 minutes,\nincluding recipe thumbnails, cancelled unsaved-image navigation, unchanged household defaults\nwhen a switch is cancelled, and an independently created ingredient conflict fixture.\n\nA real container restart preserved canonical authenticated API responses for admin and the\ndedicated test account across 21 household memberships. SHA-256 comparisons confirmed all\n120 persisted files unchanged; nine currently referenced images were also retrieved and\nchecked for exact bytes, private cache policy and no-sniff headers. Enabled state and household\naccess recovered without a manual enable hook. Private payloads were not printed.\n\nRootless TCP and Unix-socket smoke tests passed, including creation of a household ingredient\nand recipe and mode-0600 verification of the overlay. Production image build uses Rust 1.85.\n\nPrivate pre-change copies remain under ignored var/nextcloud/backups. Seventeen old strictly\nrecognised synthetic browser-fixture memberships were retired from the admin selector, with\nownership/data retained by the dedicated test account; four admin households remain. Fixtures\nwith unrecognised profile names, recipe titles or other members were excluded from this cleanup.\nNo existing Nextcloud data reset or AGENTS.md changes.\n\nRepository gates and client audit passed locally. Core implementation commit ce6e2e1 passed\nall ten GitHub CI checks, including image/transport tests, client types/build/audit, Rust quality\nand coverage, MSRV, both build profiles, licences, advisories, SBOM and metrics. Final evidence\nand additional JPEG/WebP fixtures use the same enforced gates; current-head results are tracked\nin [PR #18](https://github.com/Th3Link/mealshop/pull/18). These checks do not establish formal WCAG\ncertification, a live calendar provider or nutrient composition for household declarations.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0024_nextcloud_daily_workflows_validation_md {}

#[doc = "# Ingredient organization and nutrient declarations\n\nStatus: Accepted\n\n## Context\n\nThe customer needs ingredient groups, subtypes, editable nutrient values and dietary classification.\nExisting catalogue records have exact source identities, while recipe revisions pin their effective inputs.\nThe household overlay already provides private storage, writer checks and optimistic revisions.\n\n## Alternatives\n\n- Rewrite the curated catalogue or reuse a nearby flour's nutrient values: breaks source identity.\n- Treat groups as composition: implies food membership instead of organizational hierarchy.\n- Automatically inherit every value and dietary label: conceals uncertainty and explicit user choices.\n- Add a separate persistence adapter or framework: unnecessary for this slice.\n\n## Decision\n\nExtend the existing household overlay with one-level organization and explicit reference/own/inherit\nnutrition modes. Preserve primary sources separately when applying household overrides. Pin both the\nparent and effective values in recipe revisions. No new crates or API routes are required.\n\nDietary class and origin are separate explicit enums: vegetarian food may still have animal origin.\nThese declarations do not clear allergies or override hard dietary constraints. Only nutrient values\ninherit; classifications remain explicit per ingredient. Unknown values stay unknown, including the\nretrieval date of newly declared nutrient profiles. Salt and sodium remain independent quantities.\n\n## Consequences\n\nPrimary catalogue files remain untouched, existing flour identities remain searchable, and historical\nrecipes do not change after group edits. Old overlays load through defaults; writes retain their current\nrevision and private atomic-storage protocol. Older application versions require a matching pre-upgrade\nbackup to read data written with organization fields. Arbitrarily nested organizational trees are outside\nthis accepted one-level slice.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0025_ingredient_groups_adrs_md {}

