#[doc = "# Ingredient groups, declared nutrition and classification\n\nStatus: Done\nOrigin: Customer, after PR #18 merge\n\n1. Household ingredients form explicit groups with one level of subtypes. Existing wheat, rye and spelt flour records are organised without changing identities or copying nutrient profiles.\n2. Editors can enter exact decimal nutrient values per 100 g, with named units, source/evidence notes and explicit unknowns. Readers cannot edit. Existing primary records and historical recipes retain their sources.\n3. Subtypes explicitly choose reference, own or inherited nutrition. Inherited data retains its group identity and declaration provenance; missing values remain unknown. Recipe revisions pin the effective values and group so subsequent changes cannot rewrite old calculations.\n4. Dietary class (unknown/vegan/vegetarian/meat or fish) and origin (unknown/plant/animal/mixed) are separate, explicit declarations. They do not replace allergens or establish safety.\n5. Grouped browsing, subtype search and recipe selection remain native, responsive and keyboard accessible. Existing annotations, favourites and archive actions preserve group/nutrition data.\n6. Validate references, prevent hierarchy cycles, retain quantities and enforce existing revision/permission checks. Verify persistence, recipe calculations and real Nextcloud flows.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0025_ingredient_groups_specification_md {}

#[doc = "# UX\n\nShow groups as expandable native ingredient lists with subtype counts; searching a type keeps its parent context. Use the same parent-qualified names in recipe selection. The ingredient editor adds group/type controls, a distinct dietary/origin section, and a nutrient table with units per 100 g. Empty numeric fields mean unknown; zero is an explicit value. Inheritance is opt-in and clearly labelled. Existing primary references are preserved separately from household-declared effective values.\n\n\nExisting native Nextcloud components, typography and theme tokens take priority. UX UI Pro Max is\nused for labelled forms, progressive disclosure and derived Vue state; Taste contributes alignment,\nspacing and screenshot review only. Its website hero, palette, font, navigation and effects generators\nare deliberately excluded by the customer's native-app constraints. No separate design system or\nvalidation library is introduced. Numeric fields appear only for an own profile; inherited values are\nlabelled in the ingredient detail. Automated browser checks run inside the real embedded Nextcloud\nshell, not an isolated marketing-page gate. Archived parents retain their identity in editors and do not\nhide active subtypes. The ingredient edit action explicitly includes all ingredient metadata.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0025_ingredient_groups_ux_notes_md {}

#[doc = "# Acceptance evidence\n\nEnvironment: existing Nextcloud 35.0.2 with `AppAPI` 35.0.0 at the customer-authorized local\naddress. Existing manual-install registration, secret and private data directory were retained.\nThe test image runs as UID/GID 1000 with a read-only root filesystem. No data reset or AGENTS.md edit.\n\n| Acceptance | Evidence |\n| --- | --- |\n| AC 1: groups and exact identities | Existing wheat/rye/spelt exact IDs are grouped; `ingredient-groups.spec.ts` exercises creating and finding a group and subtype. Offline catalogue import/verifier still passes with 313 unchanged primary/identity records. |\n| AC 2: exact declared nutrients and permissions | `ingredient_profiles_reject_invalid_inputs_and_preserve_primary_sources` checks reader denial, exact 1.250000, explicit zero, absent unknowns and retained original source. Negative amounts and unsupported source URLs fail. |\n| AC 3: explicit inheritance and pinned revisions | `subtype_nutrition_is_explicit_pinned_and_persistent` calculates 21 g protein from an explicitly inherited 10.5 g/100 g profile and 200 g recipe; changing the group to 20 g changes the live subtype but leaves the saved recipe unchanged across restart. |\n| AC 4: dietary/origin declarations | Backend enum validation and the browser workflow exercise vegan/plant declarations; the detail shows both independently. Existing hard-exclusion/composition/planning tests still pass. |\n| AC 5: native browsing and editing | Browser workflow checks native editor controls, own/inherit modes, reload, mobile bounds and automated WCAG 2/2.1/2.2 A/AA tags. Existing focus, invitation, localized quantity, light/dark and reduced-motion workflows remain in the full suite. |\n| AC 6: hierarchy, revisions and persistence | Invalid parents, self references and group/subtype cycles are rejected; duplicate nutrient keys fail. Existing concurrent ingredient/plan and stale-writer tests still pass. Legacy favourite updates preserve organization. Real authenticated restart/API/file checks are recorded below. |\n\n## Executed checks\n\n- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings` and\n  `cargo nextest run --workspace --locked`: 52 tests passed. A deliberately inverted parent\n  validation condition was detected by the subtype calculation/persistence test; original code restored.\n- Client strict checking, production build, formatting and all five unit tests passed.\n  Production output is approximately 358 kB gzip JavaScript and 18.3 kB gzip CSS, with no new packages.\n- Full real embedded Nextcloud browser suite passed all seven workflows together in approximately\n  1.8 minutes. The group form had no automated WCAG-tag violations; screenshots at 390 and 1440 px\n  were inspected. No application console errors occurred in the group workflow.\n- Rootless TCP and Unix-socket container smoke tests passed lifecycle, assets, auth, CSRF and private storage.\n- Real container restart preserved canonical authenticated APIs and SHA-256 hashes of 141 persisted\n  files across 23 memberships; eleven referenced images retained exact bytes and private response headers.\n- Offline import/catalogue, reference-conversion and allergen verifiers, demo i18n, Rust format,\n  licence and `RustSec` gates passed. Client audit reported zero vulnerabilities.\n\n## Final review\n\nThe final archive-parent workflow passed separately in 18.8 seconds: archiving a group leaves\nactive subtypes visible and preserves their selected archived parent in the editor. Core implementation commit 723af6f passed all ten PR checks, including Rust 1.85 image\nbuild/transport verification, coverage, both build profiles, client types/build/audit, MSRV, licences,\nadvisories, SBOM and binary metrics. Current-head checks are tracked in\n[PR #19](https://github.com/Th3Link/mealshop/pull/19). Browser evidence is scoped to tested flows and sizes; it does not claim formal WCAG\ncertification. Classifications are household statements, not inferred safety, and no nutrient value\nis inferred from a neighbouring ingredient or converted implicitly between sodium and salt.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0025_ingredient_groups_validation_md {}

#[doc = "# Decisions\n\nStatus: Accepted\n\nExtend recipe records with optional stable line IDs and part IDs, named recipe-owned parts, and step references. Keep the flattened ingredient lines as the single calculation/shopping source; parts organize them without duplicating amounts. A part may use earlier prepared parts via an acyclic dependency list. Imported/independently versioned subrecipe references are outside this customer example and not silently assumed.\n\nKeep beta-glucan and soluble fibre serialized under their existing stable vocabulary for compatibility, but expose them through a distinct optional-constituent category and result section. Missing constituent values stay unknown. This avoids rewriting frozen source records or old recipes.\n\nSorbitol is not added to the regulated fourteen-allergen source mapping. A separate trigger registry and explicit household declarations feed the existing conservative constraint review. Source: [NHS](https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/irritable-bowel-syndrome-ibs/diet-lifestyle-and-medicines/) (classification context only; no medical recommendation in the product).\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0026_authoring_experience_adrs_md {}

#[doc = "# Plan\n\nStatus: Done\n\n- [x] Persistent recipe parts, line/step associations and graph validation; exact existing calculations unchanged.\n- [x] Optional constituent category and sorbitol trigger declarations with conservative constraints.\n- [x] Recompose native forms, selectors, direct ingredient creation and recipe authoring.\n- [x] Real-browser visual/keyboard/theme checks, backend persistence/security checks and repository gates/CI.\n- [x] Begin full catalogue grouping only after this slice passes its checks.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0026_authoring_experience_plan_md {}

#[doc = "# Comfortable native authoring and recipe structure\n\nStatus: Done\nOrigin: Customer screenshots and clarification after PR #19\n\n1. Use native Nextcloud controls with persistent readable labels, clear section hierarchy, consistent input sizes, unclipped selection names and translated empty states. Preserve keyboard/focus, responsive light/dark operation and drafts.\n2. Recipe ingredient search offers creating the entered ingredient directly as a selectable result. The dialog pre-fills its name and returns it to the same row without losing quantities or the recipe. Remove the separate inline-create button.\n3. Optional food constituents are added individually with exact quantities per 100 g, evidence and unknown states. Beta-glucan and soluble fibre appear in their own category, outside ordinary nutrient entry and results. Existing values and recipe snapshots stay readable. Aggregate selected constituents across recipe ingredients and servings without inferring absence as zero or claiming a health effect.\n4. Sorbitol is an explicitly selectable intolerance trigger in ingredients and household profiles, distinct from the fourteen regulated allergen groups. Declared presence blocks affected attendees through composition and pinned snapshots; absence remains unknown.\n5. Named recipe parts act as recipe-owned subrecipes, each owning ingredient lines and steps. Steps can reference exact ingredient rows and previously prepared parts. Parts can depend on other parts; reject unknown references, duplicate identities and cycles. All ingredients are counted exactly once for nutrition, shopping, scaling and constraints. Persist associations across edits/restart; flat legacy recipes still load. No predefined bread phases, independent saved-recipe linking, timer scheduler or automatic cooking-loss assumptions are introduced.\n6. Complete backend, native-browser, accessibility and repository gates with preserved auth/revision/storage mechanisms. Audit surrounding app navigation, lists and forms for the same layout issues. Only after this slice is verified, organize the full existing catalogue in a separate subsequent slice.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0026_authoring_experience_specification_md {}

#[doc = "# Native productivity application\n\nThe screen's job is entering a recipe or ingredient without losing context. Nextcloud components, font, theme and navigation take precedence over website generators. UI UX Pro Max Quick Reference supplies field grouping, optional disclosure, visible labels, inline errors and focus recovery. Taste supplies aligned edges, restrained density, consistent control rhythm and screenshot inspection, without replacing the host UI with heroes, palettes, fonts or effects.\n\nIngredient editing: short identity section, explicit nutrient mode, common nutrients first, optional micronutrients, separately addable constituents, and collapsible classification/composition/provenance. Keep error drafts and announce saving. A name entered in recipe search becomes a create action in that same dropdown; cancelled creation retains the row.\n\nRecipe editing: identity, ingredients with optional named parts, and ordered steps. Each ingredient belongs to one part or the main recipe. Step selectors assign ingredient rows and prepared parts. Part removal moves its rows/steps to the main recipe and clears dangling references after confirmation. No drag-only controls. Existing time budgets remain conservative and sequential; this slice does not promise a parallel schedule.\n\nHousehold selection uses an external label and readable wrapping names; ingredient options show name and useful form context rather than truncating the middle. Native component focus styles remain intact. Test empty search, create/cancel/save, long names, German aliases, nested modal focus, own/unknown/zero values, mobile and dark mode.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0026_authoring_experience_ux_notes_md {}

#[doc = "# Acceptance evidence\n\nEnvironment: existing Nextcloud 35.0.2 / `AppAPI` 35.0.0. Private pre-upgrade copy retained;\nno reset, primary catalogue rewrite or AGENTS.md change. Browser iterations use a read-only built\nasset mount on the real rootless application container; final packaged checks are recorded in the PR.\n\n| AC | Evidence |\n| --- | --- |\n| 1–2 | `authoring-experience.spec.ts` finds Haferflocken as Oat flakes, creates a searched ingredient in place, retains recipe title/quantities, and checks the dialog with WCAG 2/2.1/2.2 A/AA tags. Screenshots cover the new dark mobile dialog and structured recipe. The subsequent editor check passes 320/390/768/1024/1440 px bounds. Native portalled menu content uses uniquely namespaced slot styles, not host-wide selectors. |\n| 3 | `optional_constituents_aggregate_exactly_and_sorbitol_blocks_pinned_recipes` checks 6 g beta-glucan and 3.75 mg of a declared custom constituent, with exact portion rounding. `constituent_identity_units_unknowns_and_legacy_values_remain_consistent` checks unknown/partial subtotals, duplicate IDs, unit conflicts and compatibility values. The browser adds an optional field and sees its recipe subtotal after reload. |\n| 4 | The same backend test checks sorbitol's pinned declaration still blocks after the current ingredient declaration is removed. Fourteen regulated allergen groups and their 106 exact positive mappings are unchanged. |\n| 5 | `recipe_parts_preserve_associations_and_reject_cycles_and_unknown_references` checks line/part/step identity, dependency cycles including step references, exact scaling, missing/duplicate references and restart equality. The browser creates two named parts, assigns lines/steps and prepared parts, saves, reloads and edits them. |\n| 6 | Full real browser suite: eight passed together in approximately 2.5 minutes, including reader/revocation/conflicts, German quantities, exact source conversions, images, calendar skips, themes and reduced motion. Backend suite: 55 passed; strict client build and seven unit tests passed. |\n\nOffline catalogue import/verification, reference conversions and allergen verification pass. Format,\nclippy, licence and advisory gates are retained. This evidence does not establish formal WCAG certification,\nmedical benefit, comprehensive intolerance coverage, or a parallel cooking/timer schedule. The broader\ncatalogue grouping is deliberately a subsequent slice after these checks.\n\nThe first authoring commit fe3c0e7 passed all ten PR CI checks. Subsequent review additionally verifies\nthat an older organization payload cannot erase new intolerance/constituent data, that replacing a\nconverted ingredient clears its old conversion evidence, and that anonymous legacy lines receive\ncollision-resistant IDs. Final combined suite: 58 backend tests and nine embedded browser workflows.\nAn inverted dependency-cycle guard and a removed group assignment were both detected by behavioral\ntests; original source restored before rerunning the complete suite.\n"]
