#[doc = "# Complete catalogue organization\n\nStatus: Done\nOrigin: Customer; explicitly after the native authoring improvements\n\n1. After F26 passes its behavioral checks, assign every bundled ingredient ID to one explicit, human-readable organizational group. Preserve the existing wheat/rye/spelt flour group IDs and every source identity, value, form, translation and unknown state.\n2. Use one-level culinary groups that distinguish useful variants (flours, milk, quark, tofu, oils, rice and similar families) without asserting shared nutrition, allergy status or composition. All primary/reference values stay on their original records.\n3. Grouped browsing shows readable group names, subtype counts and a clear expansion action. Search still exposes matching subtypes and their parent context, including compound spellings. Group metadata remains editable through its detail view.\n4. Offline verification proves complete, unique exact-ID coverage, valid bilingual group metadata and no invented nutrient profiles. Custom replacement catalogues are grouped only for mapped IDs actually present; unknown IDs remain unmodified.\n5. Existing household overrides, pinned recipes, constraints, reverse lookup, source conversions and quantity precision remain intact. Verify the final packaged app, browser workflows, persistence, required repository gates and CI.\n"]
