#[doc = "# Unified meal planning, preparation and ingredient extensions\n\nStatus: Done\nPriority: Must\nMilestone: M2\nOrigin: Customer-approved visual concepts, 2026-11-10; implementation explicitly authorized.\n\n## Acceptance contract\n1. One native Nextcloud meal-plan calendar contains meals and their advance preparation. Normal cooking, mealprep and multi-day bread use the same workflow. No separate calendar or mandatory mealprep mode.\n2. A preparation pins a recipe revision and production serving count. Its meal allocations may span days; allocated servings cannot exceed production. Shopping counts production once, including unallocated portions. Moving a meal must not duplicate production or its shopping contribution. Existing attendee exclusions, revision checks and purchase provenance remain enforced.\n3. Recipe-owned parts own their ingredient lines and steps in the editor. Parts reference prepared parts, not duplicate their ingredient mass. Flat recipes remain simple and legacy records remain readable. Native controls, translations, draft protection and keyboard operation apply.\n4. Recipe ingredient lines accept optional typed preparation extensions. Initial type: temperature, exact signed decimal Celsius with preserved original input and explicit provenance (recipe author declaration, not a device measurement). It does not alter ingredient identity, mass, nutrition, shopping or serving scaling. Malformed, duplicate and unsupported extensions are rejected. Saved revisions and subsequent edits preserve extensions.\n5. Calendar preparation reminders and actual cooking completion are distinct. Completing mixing starts the preset waiting timer from the actual action, e.g. 07:08 + 45 min = 07:53. Parallel recipe parts must retain their relationship. No mandatory sourdough readiness assessment.\n6. Approved concept screens are retained in this folder, labelled as design references, not implementation evidence. Validate real Nextcloud workflows, API persistence/negative cases, production-once shopping, client checks and repository gate before completion.\n\n## Boundaries\nNo scale driver, device discovery, remote heating control or promised device protocol. Structured values are available in the existing versioned recipe JSON for a later separately specified integration. No invented cooking, cooling or storage durations; Celsius targets are instructions, not food-safety guarantees. Existing source quantities and unreviewed source content remain intact.\n\n## Reference acceptance examples\nBrotkruste: four prepared parts feed the main dough; water can retain 150 g plus a declared 60 °C target. Initial sourdough/brühstück/oat preparations start together; a calendar anchor schedules continuing with spelt at 07:00. Curry: four portions produced once Wednesday, two allocated Thursday and two Friday. Empty/unassigned production portions remain visible.\n\nImplementation evidence: [validation.md](../page_specs_0031_unified_preparation_validation_md/index.html). Actual browser screenshots are in\n[verification/](../page_specs_0031_unified_preparation_verification_readme_md/index.html); approved drawings remain in [screens/](../page_specs_0031_unified_preparation_screens_readme_md/index.html).\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0031_unified_preparation_specification_md {}

#[doc = "# Approved native interaction contract\n\nNextcloud owns shell, typography, theme, labels and focus. Keep its existing left navigation. The meal plan is the only calendar. Show preparation in the same days as meal allocations. A native detail panel edits production and eating dates. Adding another eating day uses the same entry, without duplicating shopping.\n\nEach recipe part expands locally to ingredient rows and its instructions. Prepared parts are selected by stable reference. Additional ingredients remain separate. Temperatures belong to ingredient rows under an optional extension action: type Temperature, exact value, Celsius. Unknown extensions remain absent, never inferred from text. Show the stored value in recipe reading and cooking context; preserve it through edits and quantity scaling.\n\nOne completion action starts the waiting timer at the actual time. Planned notifications only open the relevant task. Unknown durations stay unknown. Range handling and overlap conflicts must be explicit, not silently flattened.\n\n## Approved visual references\nThe German PNGs in screens/ are customer-approved design evidence. They are intentionally retained in their reviewed language; canonical specification and coded keys remain English. They are drawings, not screenshots of completed implementation. General and multi-part examples both apply. Responsive implementation must stack detail forms, retain readable ingredient names and support keyboard alternatives to dragging.\n\n## Implementation choices for review\nExisting time budgets remain available in one collapsed “Limit available time” section. New native plans use the API's supported upper bounds (24 h active, 24 h elapsed plus 30 days advance); a bread recipe is not rejected by an invented default one-hour budget. These are validation limits, not promised user availability or duration estimates. Existing explicit budgets remain intact. A later timing contract may distinguish unset budgets structurally.\n\nExisting entries keep their production identity hidden while editing eating dates through allocations. Removing the final allocation persists an explicit empty list, rather than silently converting it into a full-quantity meal. The shared calendar still shows the unassigned production. Dietary review remains conservative across all allocated days.\n\nA calendar anchor is a planned reminder, not a lock on actual work. The user may complete work earlier; explicit reviewed delays and unfinished prerequisites remain separate constraints.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0031_unified_preparation_ux_notes_md {}

#[doc = "# F31 acceptance evidence\n\nStatus: Done — accepted native Nextcloud scope.\n\nTarget: actual Nextcloud 35.0.2 / `AppAPI` 35.0.0, native Vue 3 client and protected Rust backend.\nApproved PNGs in screens/ remain design references, separate from actual browser screenshots.\n\n| AC | Observable evidence |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | `e2e/unified-preparation.spec.ts` creates preparation and eating allocations in one calendar and opens the linked cooking schedule. Existing daily/calendar tests cover flat meals and skipped attendees. |\n| 2 | Four portions are produced once, allocated two per eating day, then moved without duplicating the synchronized `100.000002 g`. Planning API tests cover restart, empty allocations, over-allocation, duplicate/occupied slots, revisions and immutable shopping provenance. |\n| 3 | Native authoring tests create ingredient/step groups with stable prepared-part references, retain the parent draft during inline ingredient creation, then reopen the saved revision. |\n| 4 | API tests preserve exact original Celsius spelling through save/reopen, scaling and restart, rejecting malformed/duplicate/unsupported extensions. The browser saves, edits and reads `60.000001 °C` in cooking without changing mass or identity. |\n| 5 | API tests anchor planned work at 07:00 but start a 45-minute wait from actual 07:08 completion, ending at 07:53. The browser starts a one-second wait after work with a 120-second estimate, then advances the dependent part without a readiness assessment. Independent timers, offline/reload recovery and multi-day scheduling remain covered. |\n| 6 | Nine approved concept PNGs are retained. Actual embedded workflows, API tests, client checks and the repository gate provide implementation evidence. |\n\n## Checks and native review\nCatalogue import/verifier, conversion/allergen verifiers and Node i18n passed. Rust formatting,\nworkspace Clippy with warnings denied, 88 nextest tests (zero skipped), licence policy, `RustSec`\naudit and strict rustdoc passed. Locked Node 24.15 / npm 12.2.2 client formatting, strict Vue/`TypeScript`\nbuild, 16 unit tests and npm audit (zero vulnerabilities) passed. The full installed-container embedded suite\npassed all 19 tests. The final shopping-only label refinement separately passed the four existing\nshopping contracts and its visual/localization test. Rootless container smoke tests\npassed for TCP and Unix sockets: lifecycle, assets, auth/CSRF, private shopping/products and cooking.\n\nThe sidebar has one native title, distinct production/allocation labels and focus after its opening\ntransition. A completed preview receives focus. Native dialogs use their close lifecycle, draft\nprotection and connected invoker focus restoration. The timer regression explicitly holds an old\nbackground response, proving pause refresh before that response returns rather than using a speed\nthreshold. Reviewed precision/provenance, legacy defaults, household authorization/revisions,\nbounded allocations, source stability, dependency cycles, persistence and production-once shopping.\nNo dependency or crate was added.\n\n## Operations and limits\nAn actual container restart preserved authenticated API snapshots, cooking deadlines/timer states and\n35 persisted files (11 memberships, one referenced image). Verified fixture archival then retained both\ncustomer memberships and their eight files byte-for-byte against the initial PR #27 backup. The final repeat passed; only ledger/content-verified synthetic\nhouseholds and their identified reminders are archived. Both customer households remain active, with\nmonotonic IDs preserved. The final documentation-only image rebuild retains verified frontend bytes\nand is checked before handoff. Complete private backups and the original functional image remain available.\nNever run host/container writers concurrently or use customer households as acceptance fixtures.\n\nOne shared attendee list conservatively applies to all eating allocations. Calendar anchors are\nplanned reminders; author temperatures and elapsed waits establish neither device measurements nor\nfood readiness. Physical scale/heater integration, guaranteed device alerts and standalone/Flutter\nclients remain outside this slice. Remote CI must pass on the exact PR head before handoff.\n\nActual [calendar/cooking screenshots](../page_specs_0031_unified_preparation_verification_readme_md/index.html) were reviewed; an additional read-only\ncalendar check passed four widths and the WCAG-tagged axe audit.\n"]
