#[doc = "# Visual household shopping\n\nStatus: Done\nPriority: Must\nOrigin: Customer request and supplied Bring reference, 2026-11-10.\nMilestone: M2\n\n## User value\nRecognize groceries quickly, check them off with one tap and add missing goods without navigating away.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. The existing native household shopping destination presents open and purchased goods as responsive, named tiles with consistent decorative icons and exact quantities. One tap checks/unchecks an item. Text and check state accompany color.\n2. A labelled search retains input focus while filtering translated names. Adding a named item from search opens an inline exact-quantity form; successful saving restores discovery focus. No quantity or ingredient identity is inferred from a name.\n3. The last successful check-off can be undone immediately. Errors retain confirmed server state and do not announce success; mutations keep existing writer/revision checks.\n4. Item details retain all recipe/production contributions, purchase receipts, shop assignment/fallback and keyboard ordering. Searching cannot silently replace a complete shop order with a filtered subset.\n5. Real embedded Nextcloud verification covers keyboard/focus, reader access, failed writes, light/dark, reduced motion and 320/390/768/1440 widths. No customer household is a fixture. Existing F31 mealprep behavior remains intact.\n\n## Boundaries\nThe reference supplies interaction direction, not brand colors, illustrations, fonts or a replacement shell. Nextcloud components/tokens take precedence. No fake recent-use history, automatic restock, new backend endpoints, quantities, nutrition or allergy classification.\n\n## Links\nImplementation: [plan.md](../page_specs_0032_visual_shopping_plan_md/index.html). Interaction contract: [ux-notes.md](../page_specs_0032_visual_shopping_ux_notes_md/index.html). Decisions: [adrs.md](../page_specs_0032_visual_shopping_adrs_md/index.html).\nAcceptance evidence: [validation.md](../page_specs_0032_visual_shopping_validation_md/index.html). Actual browser screenshots: [screens/](../page_specs_0032_visual_shopping_screens_readme_md/index.html).\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0032_visual_shopping_specification_md {}

#[doc = "# Native shopping interaction contract\n\nThe screen's job is finding the next item and marking it purchased. The customer-supplied Bring image\ninforms compact item tiles, an obvious search/entry point and separated purchased goods. Rebuild these\npatterns with native Nextcloud checkboxes, buttons, dialog, colors and fonts. Use the existing MDI family;\nicons are decorative category cues from explicit linked ingredient metadata, never dietary declarations.\nAn unlinked item has the generic basket icon. Quantities remain exact and visibly qualified by unit.\n\nKeep tile labels wrapping to two lines and the whole checkbox area tappable. Full names remain in\naccessible labels, desktop titles and item details; exact quantities are never truncated. Use at least\n44px check-off targets and 8px gaps; retain the host's native action controls.\nMove provenance and shop controls into a named dialog, leaving a separate, labelled details action on\neach tile. Keep details reachable in shopping mode. A search is a cached derived view; it never changes\nshopping data or order. Clear the search before reordering a shop so hidden items cannot be dropped.\nTiles stay inert until the native detail dialog finishes closing, including its final transition frame.\n\nSearch sits above the tiles. Its add action pre-fills only the item label and reveals a compact inline\nform with the existing explicit quantity/unit fields and optional confirmed ingredient link. Enter and\nEscape work without throwing away a changed draft. Successful add clears search, restores its focus\nand shows the saved item; failures retain input. A last successful check/uncheck exposes Undo. Checking\nadvances keyboard focus to the next visible open item, or the purchased disclosure; unchecking reveals\nthe restored item. Do not optimistically claim purchases before the server accepts them.\n\nUX-UI-Pro-Max's verified touch-spacing and Vue computed-state guidance applies. Taste informs equal\nedges, concise hierarchy, icon consistency and screenshot refinement. Its marketing layout, palette,\nfont, animation and standalone checker requirements are overridden by the customer's native Nextcloud\nhierarchy and real embedded browser acceptance. No marketing kit or global reset is introduced.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0032_visual_shopping_ux_notes_md {}

#[doc = "# F32 acceptance evidence\n\nStatus: Done — accepted native Nextcloud scope.\n\nTarget: embedded Nextcloud 35.0.2 / `AppAPI` 35.0.0 and `@nextcloud/vue` 9.14.1. The Bring reference\ninforms discovery and compact tiles; host colors, fonts, icons, navigation and controls remain native.\n\n| AC | Observable verification |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Named native checkbox tiles retain exact quantities, decorative icons from explicit metadata, text/check state and purchased goods. Pointer/keyboard checks, unchecking and provenance are covered by visual/shopping browser tests. |\n| 2 | Search retains focus and finds canonical/translated names. Enter pre-fills only a label. Explicit `0.100001 kg` persists as `100.001 g`, retaining original quantity in details. Saving restores search focus; no ingredient identity, quantity or recent-use history is inferred. |\n| 3 | Confirmed checks expose Undo and restore focus. An injected 503 retains confirmed unchecked state; retry reloads it. A delayed successful write disables controls without moving the tile. Reload clears stale Undo context. |\n| 4 | Existing tests retain contributions, purchased receipts, recipe rescaling/plan sync, shops/fallback, keyboard ordering and consented history. Search disables ordering instead of replacing a complete shop order with a subset. Barcode/manual-entry/camera-stop fallbacks remain covered. |\n| 5 | Real isolated Chromium uses the Nextcloud shell/proxy and ledger-recorded synthetic households. Light/dark, reduced motion, keyboard/focus, reader restrictions and 320/390/768/1440 widths are covered. Tested states have no axe violations for WCAG 2/2.1/2.2 AA tags. F31 mealprep remains covered. |\n\n## Visual and behavior review\nScreenshots exposed unequal native checkbox widths, symbol/check overlap and bad long-name clipping.\nTiles now fill their cells, reserve the checkbox corner and wrap names to two lines. Full names stay\naccessible and available in details; quantities remain complete. Mobile uses three columns at\n360–600px and two below that. No custom palette, fonts, reset or new framework was introduced.\n\nThe delayed-save regression initially measured a 28px tile jump when the page spinner appeared.\nInitial loading retains that spinner; list mutations use the existing status region and native busy\ncontrols. No optimistic purchase acknowledgement is used. The installed-container full suite passed\n19 tests; after the final label-only refinement, all four existing shopping contracts and the\nvisual/localization test passed. German status labels additionally remain on one line at the narrowest\nthree-column width, 360px.\nBackground tiles remain inert through the native dialog's complete close lifecycle. The shopping\nworkflow immediately reopens item details after shop assignment/filtering, guarding against a new\nopen request being lost during the close transition. Learning consent waits for the actual enabled\ncheckbox and confirms its saved checked state before starting a session.\n\n## Checks and measured cost\nRepository/client gates passed: 88 Rust tests, 16 client tests, strict types/build/format, licences and\nboth dependency audits. Unit tests cover exact zero versus a remaining microgram, translated all-word\nmatching, stable identity/order and neutral unlinked icons. Temporarily inverting the zero predicate\nmakes the new test fail; the original was restored before verification.\n\nLocked JavaScript is 1,367,492 bytes versus 1,354,731 in the original PR #27 image. The same Python\ngzip level 9 with zero mtime gives 419,997 versus 415,154 bytes (+4,843 bytes). This measures bundle\nsize, not page-load improvement. No dependency, crate, endpoint or persisted model was added.\nSearch and ingredient lookup are computed from existing data.\n\n## Operations and limits\nComplete private backups precede installation and fixture archival. Customer households are excluded\nusing recorded identity and content checks. A real restart retained API snapshots, deadlines/timers and 35 files (11 memberships, one image).\nVerified fixture archival preserved both customer membership rows and all eight customer files against\nthe initial backup. Final image assets are compared byte-for-byte with the independent locked build,\nwith rootless TCP/Unix smoke and health checks before handoff. Axe supports accessibility review; universal conformance and physical camera coverage\nare not claimed. Remote CI is checked on the exact PR head before handoff.\n\nActual [English/German screenshots](../page_specs_0032_visual_shopping_screens_readme_md/index.html) were inspected. The German follow-up also\npasses its WCAG-tagged axe audit. CI must pass on the exact PR head; no advisory ignores were added.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0032_visual_shopping_validation_md {}

