#[doc = "# Compact recipes and explicit homemade ingredients\n\nStatus: Done\nPriority: Must\nMilestone: M2\nOrigin: Customer corrections to F31 recipe display/editing, 2026-11-10.\n\n1. Match the approved recipe references with compact ingredient rows and desktop ingredients/instructions side by side. Parts, metadata and instructions remain expanded; no disclosure is needed to read/edit the recipe. Stack naturally on narrow screens.\n2. Show ingredient/quantity/unit column labels once. Retain accessible row labels, complete selection names, exact values and keyboard operation. Row-end trash removes a line. Optional ingredient actions live behind a labelled native plus menu; adding temperature is one such action, without a repeated temperature invitation or a water-specific rule.\n3. Buying remains the legacy default. A recipe may explicitly reference a recipe-owned preparation part for a homemade ingredient using optional `prepared_part` on its ingredient line. No global availability is inferred from a food name. The user declares that part's measured base ingredients and instructions; no recipe, yield or conversion is invented.\n4. The finished reference retains its original declared mass/input, identity and source snapshot. Only measured base lines count toward nutrition, constituents, shopping and meal-plan deltas, exactly once. Nutrition explicitly reports unmodelled cooking/yield. All identities, including prepared references, remain in conservative dietary review; homemade never bypasses hard exclusions.\n5. Validate existing parts, nonempty transitive base ingredients and instructions, one output line per preparation, and cycles across all dependency kinds. Invalid/stale/read-only writes leave persisted state unchanged. Saved revisions, scaling, reopen and cooking retain preparation references. Cooking depends on the corresponding preparation steps.\n6. Creating a preparation keeps the current draft and adds a visible part to complete. Switching a simple preparation back to purchased, or removing its output, confirms removal of that preparation's inputs/steps. Referenced/nested preparations require resolving dependencies first; do not silently discard shared work. Legacy flat recipes retain behavior.\n7. Verify actual embedded Nextcloud recipe editing/reading, both languages/themes, keyboard, exact scaling, inline creation, homemade shopping and cooking, 320/390/768/1440 widths, axe, repository/client/container gates and restart. Preserve customer data and archive only verified own fixtures.\n\nSee [UX contract](../page_specs_0033_compact_recipe_preparation_ux_notes_md/index.html), [decisions](../page_specs_0033_compact_recipe_preparation_adrs_md/index.html) and [delivery plan](../page_specs_0033_compact_recipe_preparation_plan_md/index.html).\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0033_compact_recipe_preparation_specification_md {}

#[doc = "# Native recipe interaction contract\n\nThe customer overrides the older concept's collapsed secondary parts: every part remains open.\nUse the approved compact row proportions and two-column composition, retaining Nextcloud controls,\ncolors/fonts and visible section/column labels. Individual row labels remain available to assistive\ntechnology without repeating visible “Choose ingredient”. Exact conversion evidence stays visible\nwhen a non-mass unit requires it. Optional added fields remain visible once present.\n\nA plus action per ingredient opens native actions for temperature or homemade preparation. No\nwater-only shortcut, dietary inference or preset bread phases. Existing temperatures display inline;\nremove uses a labelled icon. Parts own their ingredient/step lists, with compact preparation timing,\nvisible associations and a clear title. On mobile the columns stack without horizontal overflow.\n\nHomemade is an explicit recipe choice. Its preparation part requests actual input ingredients and\ninstructions; the finished reference is labelled and links to that part. Buying again confirms the\nremoval of a simple, unshared preparation. Shared/nested dependencies block destructive conversion\nwith an actionable explanation. Original declared output and source facts remain distinct from input\nnutrition; no cooking loss or yield is inferred. Read mode mirrors the same open section hierarchy.\n\nApply UX-UI-Pro-Max for task flow, Taste for density/alignment and frontend engineering for accessible\ncontrols and stable IDs. The native Nextcloud hierarchy overrides other palettes, fonts and kits.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0033_compact_recipe_preparation_ux_notes_md {}

#[doc = "# F33 acceptance evidence\n\nTarget: native embedded Nextcloud 35.0.2 / `AppAPI` 35.0.0, Vue 3 and `@nextcloud/vue` 9.14.1.\nThe customer supersedes the older screens' collapsed parts: every recipe section remains open.\n\n| AC | Observable verification |\n|---|---|\n| 1–2 | Real `compact-recipes.spec.ts` and updated authoring/preparation workflows exercise open parts, shared headers, accessible hidden row labels, inline ingredient creation, native plus menus, temperature editing and row trash. Desktop ingredients/instructions share a row; narrow layouts stack. |\n| 3–4 | `homemade_parts_keep_declared_outputs_but_calculate_only_base_inputs` preserves original output quantity/source identity through revisions, scale and reopen, while nutrients/constituents use measured inputs. Stateless unresolved calculations fail. Display names come from the frozen catalogue, including outputs omitted from nutrient contributions. |\n| 4–5 | `homemade_ingredients_purchase_only_inputs_and_keep_dietary_and_cooking_guards` checks exact direct shopping and idempotent plan sync, both finished/input hard exclusions, restart and main-before-producer instruction ordering. Real `AppAPI` role tests reject reader recipe writes; existing stale-write/isolation contracts remain exercised. |\n| 5–6 | Invalid unknown/empty/self/cross-cycle/multiple/zero-mass/unknown-food preparations fail. Browser checks shared-part removal guards, disabled self-dependent step moves, cancelled conversion and confirmed conversion without losing the finished amount/main instruction. New preparation quantities start blank. |\n| 7 | Embedded Chromium checks English/German, native system light/dark, reduced motion, keyboard focus, 320/390/768/1440 layouts and WCAG 2/2.1/2.2 AA axe tags. This supports an accessibility review, not a universal conformance claim. |\n\n## Visual review\nThe approved reference composition informs density and hierarchy, retaining native Nextcloud colors,\nfonts, controls and icons. Screenshots exposed native selector minimum-width overlap, clipped exact\namounts, offset trash buttons and a sticky title colliding with the navigation toggle. Scoped layout\nrules correct those issues; full amounts and the added temperature's Celsius unit remain visible.\nDraft tracking is limited to editing; fragment-only navigation keeps the draft and focuses the\npreparation region. The read toolbar groups portion preview, display unit and cooking. Metadata and source evidence remain\nopen below the core recipe; no global reset, palette, typeface or UI framework was introduced.\n\n## Checks\nRepository/client gate: catalogue import/check, catalogue/conversion/allergen/group verification,\nkeyed-message tests, Rust fmt/clippy/nextest, licences/audit, native format/types/unit/build/audit and\nstrict rustdoc. The full Rust suite contains 90 tests; the client suite contains 16 tests. Browser\ncoverage contains 20 real embedded workflows, including shopping, cooking, invitations, conflicts,\nimage persistence, exact localized quantities and mealprep.\n\n## Measured asset cost\nThe independent locked build contains 1,377,783 JavaScript bytes versus 1,367,492 in the previous\nPR #27 test image. Python gzip level 9 with zero mtime gives 422,702 versus 419,997 bytes\n(+2,705 compressed bytes). This measures asset size, not page-load speed. No dependency or crate\nwas added; preparation graphs and ingredient lines retain their existing bounded sizes.\n\n## Operational verification\nThe installed `mealshop.local/mealshop:compact-recipes` image passes all 20 browser workflows\nserially in the real Nextcloud shell. The final image passes isolated rootless TCP/Unix lifecycle,\nauthentication/CSRF, assets, private storage, shopping and cooking checks. Its JavaScript and CSS\nare byte-identical to the independent locked build. A real restart preserves authenticated API\nsnapshots, cooking states/deadlines and all 39 persisted files (12 memberships and one referenced\nimage checked), including the saved homemade recipe revision.\n\nComplete private backups precede installation and cleanup. Only verified ledger-owned synthetic\nhouseholds and their own cooking notices were archived. Both pre-existing household membership rows\nand all eight customer files match the initial snapshot; the cleaned instance starts authenticated\nwith the two original households retained. Four final [observed screens](../page_specs_0033_compact_recipe_preparation_screens_readme_md/index.html) were inspected.\n\nThe repository/client gate passes with 90 Rust tests and 16 client tests. The independent strict\nrustdoc and ingredient-group verification also pass. Remote CI is a merge gate on the exact PR head;\nthe PR records the observed check links without changing executable code to record that result.\n\nNo finished-food availability, recipe, raw/output ratio, nutrient retention, cooking loss or yield is\ninferred. Independent saved subrecipes and multi-output yield models remain outside this explicit\nrecipe-owned preparation contract. Old binaries require restoring the matching complete snapshot.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0033_compact_recipe_preparation_validation_md {}

