#[doc = "# Source-backed nutrition ranges\n\nStatus: Done\nPriority: Must\nMilestone: M2\nOrigin: Customer request, following F33, 2026-11-11.\n\n## Objective\nEvery existing food contributes meaningful available nutrition. Missing product-specific data may\nuse explicitly labelled comparative estimates with source-backed ranges, visible in yellow in recipes.\nThe customer explicitly authorizes comparative estimates; this extends F02/F23's earlier exact-only\npolicy without replacing the original primary records or inferring allergy safety.\n\n## Acceptance\n1. Audit all 313 bundled food identities and household ingredients. Provide source-backed energy,\n   protein, fat and a correctly defined carbohydrate value for every bundled food; fill further\n   supported missing nutrients using retained primary records/declarations. Keep unavailable individual\n   nutrients explicit, never invent values or treat missing data as zero. Unbounded custom inputs\n   receive a separate incomplete-nutrition warning. Audit private inputs only with explicit permission,\n   in memory without record copies or logging; preserve unknowns when no reviewed source can be matched.\n2. Separate original reported values, same-source supplemental values, comparative ranges and household\n   declared ranges. Retain food/state, per-100-g basis, original decimal facts, publisher, record/version,\n   retrieval, URL, licence status, selection rationale and method. Existing source facts win.\n3. Comparison envelopes use the observed minimum/maximum of reviewed compatible records; they are\n   comparison spans, not guaranteed bounds or statistical confidence intervals. No arbitrary percentage,\n   raw/cooked substitution, implicit density, carbohydrate-definition conversion or constituent inference.\n4. Calculate complete recipe and portion ranges with checked exact integers, preserving unrounded\n   inputs through serving changes and outward rounding at display. A wholly unbounded input makes a\n   nutrient incomplete; show a labelled covered subtotal instead of claiming a complete range.\n5. Mark affected recipe ingredients, ingredient details and affected nutrient rows in native warning\n   yellow with text/icons. Show the ranges and accessible, inspectable comparison sources in English\n   and German, system light/dark and narrow layouts. Preserve F33's compact always-open recipe sections.\n6. Household editors can explicitly enter nutrient ranges with evidence, including inherited group\n   values; readers cannot write. Organizational group ranges use their explicit members only. New\n   recipe revisions pin effective evidence. Legacy recipes gain a versioned supplemental analysis while\n   their persisted originals/history stay byte-identical; legacy fallback v1 remains immutable.\n7. Dietary constraints, ingredient identity, shopping masses and homemade input-only accounting remain\n   unchanged. Verify old/new records, scaling, malformed bounds/provenance, stale/reader writes,\n   restart and real embedded Nextcloud behavior. Audit coverage reproducibly offline, retain backups,\n   archive only owned fixtures, run all repository/client/container gates and check CI on the PR head.\n\n## Implementation boundaries\nRust/Axum remains the calculation authority; Vue 3/strict TypeScript uses native Nextcloud controls\nand keyed messages. No new dependency, provider call during app use or invented endpoint. Source\nfacts and estimation data are separate files. Sources without an explicit reuse licence retain that\nunknown status; record factual nutrition declarations only, not whole copyrighted pages.\n\nBuild/check: `cargo nextest run --workspace --locked`; `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings`;\n`npm --prefix clients/nextcloud run build`; `npm --prefix clients/nextcloud test`; the full AGENTS.md gate.\nUse a new offline estimation verifier plus existing import/catalogue checks. See plan.md and ux-notes.md.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0034_evidence_nutrition_ranges_specification_md {}

#[doc = "# Nutrition uncertainty in the native client\n\nKeep the existing recipe layout. A compact native warning-colored indicator with the word\n\"Estimated\" identifies affected inputs; color alone never carries meaning. Show aggregate/portion ranges in the existing nutrient table; keep ingredient rows compact.\nReported values remain ordinary values. An incomplete range names missing inputs and labels its\ncovered subtotal. Comparison sources, method and per-100-g facts remain inspectable below nutrition.\nUse native Nextcloud warning tokens/components, stable accessible names and exact locale formatting;\nno new palette, decorative cards, global reset or mandatory disclosure to read recipe parts.\n\nIngredient editing offers a value or an explicit lower/upper range per nutrient. Evidence remains\nrequired. Group inheritance carries ranges and source identity. Missing constituent effects remain\nseparate; neither comparative composition nor a numeric zero establishes allergen safety.\n\nUnsupported core contributions receive a separate warning, labelled \"Nutrition incomplete\".\nThey never borrow an arbitrary comparison or look like a complete zero. This applies to custom\ningredients as well. Private source review requires explicit permission and does not replace the\nincomplete state when an ingredient lacks sufficient evidence.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0034_evidence_nutrition_ranges_ux_notes_md {}

#[doc = "# Flutter client decisions\n\n[ADR 0026](../page_docs_adr_0026_flutter_phone_delivery_md/index.html) accepts five complete device-testable PRs,\nNextcloud-first login/transport and a bounded shopping offline/replay boundary. Status: Accepted.\nThe customer selected Android, requested an emulator and explicitly gave implementation Go.\n[ADR 0027](../page_docs_adr_0027_mobile_shopping_receipts_md/index.html) specifies P1 credentials, dependencies,\nprotected cache, bounded request receipts and upgrade/downgrade semantics.\n\nExisting decisions remain authoritative: stack (0001), quantities (0002), persistence boundaries (0003),\nlicensing/imported sharing (0004), privacy (0005), clients/localization (0007), household authority (0012),\ndurable civil-time cooking (0016), preparation (0017), nutrition ranges (0019), sharing (0020), feedback\n(0021), scoped MCP (0022), reviewed import (0023), inventory (0024) and brewing (0025).\n\nP1 uses focused `ChangeNotifier` state, official Material controls and a bounded protected record;\nOCR, native reminders and broader database choices remain decisions of their later slices. F18's unimplemented storage adapters are not silently replaced by a phone cache.\n\n## Source decision reconciliation\n\n| Original `DECISIONS.md` question | Current finding / proposed action |\n| --- | --- |\n| Stack/folder | Flutter was already selected; propose new `clients/flutter/` (P1). No current mobile source. |\n| Nextcloud/standalone API | Shared Rust domain routes exist; mobile Nextcloud login/proxy writes need proof in P1. Standalone identity remains F18/F30 scope. |\n| Roles/children/health | Household owner/editor/reader exists. Persons are not accounts; new sensitive/child-profile projections and retention require approval before P2 collection. |\n| Separate personal plans | Propose shared household plan with explicit per-person participation/alternatives; retain independent-plan extension. |\n| Pantry scope | F15 lots/transactions already exist. P3 ports them and adds explicit physical prepared-batch allocation; do not start a conflicting generic pantry. |\n| Product/nutrition sources | Existing frozen licensed catalogue and consented product lookup are reused. Exact identity, uncertainty and source-only import rules remain. |\n| OCR/AI | No provider selected; propose on-device candidates in P5. External upload needs explicit separate authorization. |\n| Offline/notifications | New mobile offline protocol required. P1 shopping receipts; P4 cooking reconciliation/local notification integration. No assumed mobile push provider. |\n| Incomplete nutrition | F34 already supports explicit bounded comparisons/unknowns; port its exact evidence semantics, never replace missing data with zero. |\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0035_flutter_mobile_client_adrs_md {}

#[doc = "# Repository audit for the mobile pack\n\nAudit date: 2026-11-13. Baseline: `fe6dd078d8db77b6ae4e55a48f78310d53487d2a` (`main`, merged PR #37).\nThis table preserves the pre-implementation baseline. P1 now adds `clients/flutter/`, Android tooling and\n`shopping/mobile` receipts; see [current P1 verification](../page_specs_0035_flutter_mobile_client_verification_md/index.html#p1-implementation-evidence).\nThis baseline is source/contract evidence, not a mobile runtime test. Existing acceptance evidence remains\nin the linked feature folders. No retained household records were inspected for this planning task.\n\n| Capability from the pack | Verified server/web state and source evidence | Mobile gap / delivery |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Flutter app / build | Absent: `clients/` contains the Nextcloud Vue client; no `pubspec.yaml` or mobile platform project. `flutter`, `dart`, `adb`, `sdkmanager` and `xcodebuild` are not on this host's PATH; Java alone is available. | P1 creates `clients/flutter/`, toolchain/CI and an installable phone app. No Flutter command has been run here. |\n| Identity / households / invitations | Nextcloud transport and current owner/editor/reader authority in `src/exapp/mod.rs`, `src/membership.rs`, `src/exapp/sharing/`; F18/F22 evidence. | P1 native login/credential lifecycle and actual proxy-write probe; device pairing is not implemented today. |\n| People / dietary rules | Partial relative to the new pack: `src/household.rs::Member` has names, allergy/intolerance notes, allergen IDs, excluded ingredients/tags and dislikes. `evaluate` enforces current hard rules. | P2 adds reviewed presets/exceptions, origin conditions and optional goal/window/prep records. Diagnosis fields, person-level health access and a progressive mobile tour are absent. |\n| Meal plans | `src/planning.rs` has pinned meals, attendees/calendar snapshots, time budgets, slot suggestions and reviewed preview/apply; F10/F11/F31. | P3 native day/week editing and a server-owned whole-week proposal. Slot ranking is not proof of a complete multi-objective weekly optimizer or recurring attendance/window policy. |\n| Shopping and product identities | `src/shopping/{api,model,sources,products,shops}.rs` and `Shopping*.vue`; manual/recipe/plan contributions, check-off/undo, shops, consented learning, manual GTIN and lookup already exist (F06/F07/F08/F32). | P1 complete native daily list and foreground sync; P5 phone camera entry. Distinct ingredient/product/request/purchase identities must remain. |\n| Offline writes / sync | Missing as a mobile protocol. Shopping `Mutation` contains only `expected_revision` and `command`; anonymous/manual source creation allocates a new ID. Purchase records are not durable client-request receipts. Current revisions protect concurrent writes. | P1 must add bounded atomic request receipts and explicit conflict policy before automatic offline retries. A fresh retry after an unknown response can otherwise duplicate intent. |\n| Recipes / ingredients / nutrition | `src/recipes.rs`, `src/recipe_api.rs`, `src/recipe_structure.rs`, `src/ingredient_api.rs`, `src/ingredients.rs`, catalogue/quantity/evidence modules; F02–F04/F23/F25–F27/F31/F33/F34. | P2 native search, manual authoring, parts/dependencies, groups/subtypes, optional ingredient creation, source ranges and recipe images. Reuse exact canonical records; do not rebuild calculations in Dart. |\n| Sharing / collections / imported rights | `src/exapp/{library,sharing}`, `src/library`; F05 pins revisions, checks recipient membership and projects imported source URLs only. | P2 native shared content/invitations and origin-aware local projection/export. Revocation cannot retract copies already viewed. |\n| Mealprep / inventory / offers | Planned production/allocations in `src/planning.rs`; exact lots, reservations and explicit stock transactions in `src/inventory/` with F15/F31 evidence. | P3 complete mobile stock/offer workflows and the pack's physical prepared-batch/storage lifecycle. Planned mealprep is not finished physical inventory or automatic safe-expiry guidance. |\n| Cooking / timers / brewing | `src/cooking/`, `src/brewing/`, F12/F13/F14 and `Brew*.vue`; durable deadlines, calendars, source snapshots, explicit phase completion, equipment/readings. | P4 native cooking, cache/reconciliation and permission-aware local reminders; Nextcloud notification acceptance does not deliver a Flutter push notification. Cooking command retries need their own audited idempotency boundary. |\n| History / learned preferences | `src/feedback/`, F11; actual history, explicit learning epochs/consent and explained suggestions. | P4 native history/feedback/consent/reset; no claim of automatic clinical personalization. |\n| URL / OCR / video capture | `src/imports/` and F16 implement supported public URL/manual reviewed import with network/source safeguards. | P5 share-sheet integration and camera/OCR review. No mobile OCR provider, video downloader or smart-scale driver exists. |\n| Activity | No dedicated activity model/API/UI in the audited routes/models. Cooking effort/history is a different concept. | P2 optional type/duration/intensity log with explicit privacy and no fabricated kcal. |\n| Localization | Nextcloud EN/DE and exact units exist; F29 retains unfinished cross-client/versioned translations. | P1 mobile UI/exact input; extend coverage per delivery, keep source text and language-independent IDs. |\n| Standalone / hosting / other stores | Local file-backed family APIs and demo exist. Production standalone identity, hosted client admission and the SQL/Git adapter matrix are not delivered (F18/F19/F30). | Preserve future transport seams without adding unimplemented auth modes, all adapters or hosted commerce to P1. |\n\n## Actual transport and API map\n\nFor Nextcloud, preserve the installation prefix and use its authenticated `/apps/app_api/proxy/mealshop`\npath, as `clients/nextcloud/src/api.ts` and `scripts/mcp_stdio.py` already do. The domain prefix is\n`/api/households/{home}/domain`. The native app must never send the `ExApp` secret/operator token.\nThe MCP bridge demonstrates Nextcloud app-password authentication for its own route; it does not\nprove the new mobile login flow or every shopping mutation. P1 must exercise those on Nextcloud 35.\n\n| Actual path after proxy prefix | Current use / source |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/api/households`, `/api/households/{id}` and its invitation routes | Household CRUD subset/current membership; `src/exapp/mod.rs` |\n| `/api/households/{home}/collections`, `/api/shared` and sharing routes | Library and permissions; `src/exapp/{library.rs,sharing/}` |\n| `/api/ingredients`, `{domain}/api/household/ingredients` | Reference/own ingredient discovery; `src/api.rs`, `src/ingredient_api.rs` |\n| `{domain}/api/recipes`, `{domain}/api/recipes/{id}` and `/scale` | List/create/read/revise/scale; `src/recipe_api.rs` |\n| `{domain}/api/household/profiles`, `/allergens`, `/evaluate` | Profiles and dietary review; `src/household.rs` |\n| `{domain}/api/household/mealplan`, `/preview`, `/apply`, `/suggestions` | Meals and reviewed changes; `src/planning.rs` |\n| `{domain}/api/household/shopping`, `/lookup` | Current list mutations and consented lookup; `src/shopping/api.rs` |\n| `{domain}/api/household/inventory`, `/preview` | Lots/offers/stock transactions; `src/inventory/api.rs` |\n| `{domain}/api/household/cooking`, `/template`, `/preview`, `/{id}` | Durable cooking workflow; `src/cooking/api.rs` |\n| `{domain}/api/household/brewing` and recipe/batch/readings/template routes | Beverage workflows; `src/brewing/` |\n| `{domain}/api/household/history`, `/learning` | Feedback and consent; `src/feedback/api.rs` |\n| `{domain}/api/household/imports/preview`, `/imports` | Reviewed URL/manual import; `src/imports/api.rs` |\n\nPaths above describe existing route declarations, not a newly standardized mobile sync API.\nVersion/capability discovery, shopping replay receipts, expanded profiles, full-week proposals,\nphysical prepared batches and activity contracts are **proposed additions** in the corresponding PRs.\nDefine them with negative tests and migrations before use; do not fabricate current endpoints.\n"]
