#[doc = "# Flutter delivery plan — five complete phone releases\n\nStatus: P1 In progress. Customer approved Android, requested an emulator and explicitly gave the Go on 2026-11-13.\nTask/checkpoint authority: this file, following the repository's spec-folder convention. Do not\ncreate a second `tasks/` backlog or mark the imported pack's checklist as delivered.\n\n## Delivery order and scope\n\n| PR | Usable smartphone outcome | Required server work in the same PR | Dependencies |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| P1 — Connect and shop | Install app, log into Nextcloud, choose household, shop together online/offline | Mobile auth/proxy proof, capability/version contract and bounded shopping request receipts | Approved plan/Go; chosen test platform and reachable test origin |\n| P2 — People and recipe library | Guided profiles, explicit rules, recipes/ingredients/collections, optional activity | Compatible profile/rule/privacy extensions, server enforcement, activity persistence | P1; approved sensitive-data policy |\n| P3 — Household week and physical preparation | Review a whole week, swap meals, allocate mealprep/stock and update shopping | Whole-week proposal/validation, recurring attendance/windows, physical prepared-batch/stock consistency | P2 effective rules and recipe data |\n| P4 — Cook, bake and ferment | Large step mode, offline-readable recipes, timers/reminders, feedback and brew workflows | Audited cooking replay/reconciliation and native notification contract | P3 plan/stock links; P1 identity/cache/outbox |\n| P5 — Camera, share and import | Capture URL/photo/barcode, review uncertainty and save correct original-source content | Existing reviewed import plus approved OCR candidate contract only where needed | P2 authoring/provenance; approved OCR/platform capability |\n\nThese are **five implementation PRs**, not five architectural layers. Build backend, phone UI and\nverification together. Each PR may contain several small verified commits; avoid separate scaffolding,\nAPI-only, empty-navigation or last-minute “make everything work” PRs. Platform signing/CI belongs in\nP1. Larger review units are the customer's preference; internal tasks remain bounded and sequential.\n\n## P1 — Install, authenticate and complete a shopping session\n\nPhone demo: install the APK, enter a Nextcloud URL, authenticate in the system browser, choose/create a\nhousehold, add `200.000001 g` of an ingredient, check/undo, see the change in Nextcloud or a second phone,\nuse airplane mode, terminate/reopen the app, reconnect and reconcile safely. No meal plan is required.\n\n- [ ] P1.1 **Prove the transport and install path.** Set up pinned Flutter/Dart and Android CI in\n  `clients/flutter/`; choose a development application ID and stable test signing identity. Exercise\n  Login Flow v2, cancellation, expired/revoked credentials, server subpaths and real proxy GET/POST on\n  Nextcloud 35. Keep app credentials in platform-protected storage, never the `ExApp` secret. Define an\n  authenticated capability/version response as an explicitly new contract before relying on it.\n  Verify: a physical-device install/login/relaunch/sign-out; server owner/reader/denied tests;\n  the ordinary Nextcloud client still works. Likely areas: new Flutter platform/config/network modules,\n  `src/exapp/`, contract tests and CI. No unrelated authentication rewrite.\n- [x] P1.2 **Add safe offline request semantics.** Extend the existing shopping transaction with\n  bounded durable operation receipts: actor/account/household scope, immutable payload/key, expected\n  revision, atomic result and exact replay after lost responses. Revalidate current permission before\n  replay. A reused key with a different request conflicts. Existing callers retain their current\n  contract; negotiate the new capability. Record migration, capacity and downgrade/recovery behaviour.\n  Verify: apply-then-drop-response/restart/replay produces exactly one entry/purchase; two clients\n  cannot silently replace sources. Likely areas: `src/shopping/{api,model,store}.rs`, inventory receipt\n  invariants, `tests/shopping.rs`, native client compatibility tests. Receipts are not a new sync engine.\n- [x] P1.3 **Deliver the real list and persistent client outbox.** Manual items, exact units,\n  check/undo, quantities, source details, ingredient/category sections, shops/order and existing manual product entry/consented lookup.\n  Use existing ingredient groups; any new manual category metadata needs an explicit compatible contract.\n  Foreground refresh and refresh-on-resume first; no assumed WebSocket or guaranteed background worker.\n  Scope encrypted/minimized cache and outbox by canonical server/account/household.\n  Define offline retention/authorization limits; remote revocation cannot erase an offline copy.\n  Revalidate on reconnect and stop pending writes when access is removed. Represent pending,\n  confirmed, failed and conflict states separately. On account/home switch, isolate in-flight responses;\n  sign-out wipes local credentials/data. Preserve drafts on errors and reader views without write actions.\n  Verify: widget/decimal/DTO tests and two-device integration with process death and role revocation.\n\nP1 implementation evidence is recorded in [verification](../page_specs_0035_flutter_mobile_client_verification_md/index.html#p1-implementation-evidence).\nP1.1 remains unchecked for the physical-handset acceptance; the Android toolchain, emulator, browser\nlogin, protected storage, live proxy shopping and installable development APK are implemented.\n\n**P1 release gate:** downloadable installable test artifact + checksum/commit/version, installation and\nupgrade instructions, real phone evidence, Rust/native regression and Flutter gates below. Initial active\ntabs are Shopping and More, without placeholders for unimplemented flows. P1 closes F35 AC1–2 only.\n\nCritical conflict case: device A checks an item while offline; device B adds a new requirement for the\nsame ingredient. Do not replay an aggregate check against unseen new contributions. Freeze the observed\nitem/contribution scope, refresh and require reconciliation when it changes. Manual pending additions\nmust remain separate from previously purchased amounts. Do not auto-rebase financial/stock effects.\n\n## P2 — Household tour, content and optional personal activity\n\nPhone demo: create two people, one with a vegan baseline plus an explicit own-egg exception and one\nomnivore; inspect the resolved rule summary; interrupt/resume the tour; author a nested recipe, scale it,\ninspect unknown/ranged nutrients, share the allowed projection, and record a 45-minute jog without weight.\nThe diet label must reflect exceptions rather than silently claiming an unmodified vegan diet.\n\n- [ ] P2.1 **Extend effective rules and privacy together.** Resolve person-vs-account ownership,\n  child-profile access and health-field permissions/retention before collection. Keep allergies and\n  explicit exclusions hard, dislikes soft, goals optional and medical context non-prescriptive. Add\n  reviewed presets/exceptions, ingredient-origin conditions, windows/attendance/prep settings only with\n  versioned storage, validation and migration. Every new hard rule must also constrain existing\n  Nextcloud evaluation/suggestions/plan apply; do not store a rule the server then ignores.\n  Verify: conflicting presets/exceptions, unknown origin, unrelated allergy, revoked access, export/\n  deletion and legacy profile round trips; adapt existing typed Vue contracts in this same PR.\n- [ ] P2.2 **Build the resumable profile flow.** One or two questions per step, optional name/avatar capture, optional skip,\n  protected local drafts, explicit save/review and editable summary. No required diagnosis, weight or\n  calorie target. A login account and a household person remain distinct identities.\n  Verify: interruption/relaunch, no cross-person draft leakage, screen reader/large text and DE/EN.\n- [ ] P2.3 **Complete the mobile content library.** Search localized names/aliases; read/create/edit\n  recipes and ingredient groups/subtypes/nutrients/components/tags/images, with inline ingredient creation,\n  source/range/unknown presentation, portions, always-visible parts/steps, homemade inputs and cycle\n  rejection. Add collections, pinned shared revisions and invitations. Source-only imported projections\n  must also govern local cache/export/share. Share sheets for URL capture follow P5.\n  Verify: exact values and original language survive edits; restricted imports are not copied into shares;\n  reader/revocation, conflicts and unknown ingredient identities preserve the server boundary.\n- [ ] P2.4 **Add the small personal activity log.** Type, date, duration and optional intensity with\n  save/history/edit/delete, independent of food restrictions. Review permission/retention and add a\n  bounded versioned server record. Leave energy unknown without an accepted evidence/inputs model.\n  Verify: a 45-minute jog and 60-minute ride save without weight; no kcal is fabricated or used to\n  weaken hard constraints. Likely areas: profile/activity API/model, phone More/profile flows and tests.\n\n**P2 release gate:** installed P1 upgrade retains account/cache and existing user records. Recipes joins\nShopping/More; no inactive Plan/Today tab. All introduced hard rules have server enforcement evidence.\nSensitive fields stay unavailable if their separate privacy decision is not approved; report that scope\nexplicitly rather than claiming the full P2 acceptance complete.\n\n## P3 — Explainable household week, mealprep and stock\n\nPhone demo: generate/review a week for the two people, change Thursday dinner/attendance, inspect the\nshopping delta, then prepare six portions on Sunday, allocate four to later meals and retain two frozen\nportions. A plan edit must neither erase manual purchases nor count cooked production twice.\n\n- [ ] P3.1 **Implement a server-owned full-week proposal.** Reuse current evaluation, slot suggestions,\n  pinned recipes and profile/allergen revisions. Add proposal identity/expiry, per-slot confirmation,\n  effective recurring attendance/date overrides/windows and optional prep/time preferences. Explain\n  infeasibility; rank declared preferences, variety, ingredient reuse and preparation/time trade-offs.\n  Include cost only with applicable offer data and nutrition only with meaningful source coverage;\n  record the chosen criteria/limits and do not claim global optimality. Missing price/nutrition data is not zero cost/energy.\n  Verify: two-person hard-rule fixtures, impossible week, stale profile/recipe, DST/date boundaries and\n  deterministic recommendation evidence. Any new persisted constraint also protects existing web paths.\n- [ ] P3.2 **Deliver mobile Today/Plan and reviewed shopping changes.** Day/week navigation, participant/\n  portion edits and swaps preserve selected slots and protected source amounts. Show changes before\n  apply and retain drafts after concurrency failures. Today links real meals/preparation/shopping actions.\n  Verify: Thursday-only change, skipped attendee, manual/checked shopping preservation and two clients.\n- [ ] P3.3 **Unify physical batches and inventory carefully.** Extend current planned allocations and\n  exact inventory transactions for actual prepared yield, storage location, portion allocation/release,\n  leftovers, lots, offers and reversal. Track user-declared dates/conditions without invented safe shelf\n  life. No allocation exceeds recorded available quantity; planning alone cannot create physical stock.\n  Preserve ingredient/product/batch dimensions and original quantities. Verify: six = four allocated + two\n  remaining, freeze/thaw or declared storage changes, over-allocation, cancel/reversal/restart and\n  production-once shopping; keep existing F15/F31 web behaviour compatible.\n\n**P3 release gate:** all five functional tabs now exist. Upgrade the installed app and complete the\nsource pack's shared-week success journey through shopping/preparation, with current permissions and\nsource/uncertainty explanations. Fully independent personal plans remain the explicitly tracked extension.\n\n## P4 — Cooking, long preparations, fermentation and feedback\n\nPhone demo: start two timers, close/kill the app and disconnect; reopen to the original deadlines and\nstep recipe. Delay a multi-day baking task, reconcile reminders, complete actual work, book stock only\nthrough review, and inspect a separate brewing batch with its equipment/calibrated reading history.\n\n- [ ] P4.1 **Native cooking and offline recovery.** Large step UI, current-step ingredients,\n  dependencies/part relationships, actual-action waits, multiple timers and server-backed rescheduling.\n  Audit current cooking mutations; add durable operation replay where absent before queueing them.\n  Store offline intent separately and reconcile current state; never reset a timer from “now” on restart.\n  Verify: process death, clock change, overlapping timers, lost responses, explicit manual completion\n  and stale role/recipe/equipment state. Reuse the shared Rust scheduler, not a Dart scheduler copy.\n- [ ] P4.2 **Permission-aware device reminders.** Select maintained platform integration after SDK,\n  licence and OS-capability review. Schedule stable notification IDs from authoritative deadlines,\n  cancel/update on replan and reconcile on foreground/reconnect. Distinguish local reminders, server\n  delivery and acknowledged user actions. Existing Nextcloud notifications are not Flutter push.\n  Verify foreground/background/reboot and denied/revoked permissions on the supported OS versions;\n  record actual delivery limits. APNs/FCM infrastructure is a separate explicit gate, not assumed.\n- [ ] P4.3 **Complete fermentation/history integration.** Mobile brew recipes/templates, batches,\n  equipment reservations, original measurements/calibration/corrections, history/ratings, optional learning\n  consent/reset and planned-prep links. Verify concurrent physical holds, independent batches, exact\n  readings and food/brewing separation. Completion does not silently imply stock movement or safety.\n\n**P4 release gate:** the full source-pack core loop works on the phone with disclosed offline/reminder\nlimits. No medical claim or physical fermentation-complete claim follows from elapsed time.\n\n## P5 — Camera and reviewed capture\n\nPhone demo: share a supported public recipe URL, import a photo with an unresolved cup measurement,\nreview ingredient mappings/quantities, scan a product/nutrition label and recover after camera/lookup denial. Save and\nreopen the original source and reviewed values; share an imported recipe as its source link only.\n\n- [ ] P5.1 **Share-sheet and URL review.** Reuse F16 network bounds and explicit retrieval consent.\n  Mobile original/reviewed views, manual fallback, preview expiry/idempotent save and source-only\n  exports must preserve the same rules as Nextcloud. Verify blocked/private/redirect URLs and retries.\n- [ ] P5.2 **Camera/barcode and on-device OCR candidates.** Review platform/plugin/licence support and\n  privacy before dependencies. Default proposal: local OCR, explicit photo access and retained original\n  recipe and nutrition-label candidates with confidence/unknowns; no external upload. Preserve the\n  original label basis/units/definitions and review declared product values instead of copying a\n  nearby generic ingredient profile. Use manual GTIN and consented existing lookup\n  when camera support fails. Verify real phone permissions, cancellation, large/rotated images,\n  unresolved `1 cup`, exact known decimals and no silent ingredient or medical inference.\n- [ ] P5.3 **Complete the release and portability audit.** Test all enabled journeys on each supported\n  phone platform, upgrades, cache/outbox schema migrations, account removal/export and accessibility.\n  Document provider/platform limits and safe unsupported-video/manual paths. Do not add social-media\n  bypasses, scale drivers, wearables, autonomous purchases or commercial admission to finish the checklist.\n\n**P5 release gate:** all F35 acceptance criteria have real evidence. Source-pack proposals blocked by\nexternal product/provider decisions remain explicit follow-up requirements, with original criteria;\nF35 cannot be marked fully Done by silently dropping them.\n\n## Build, install and validation contract (starts with P1)\n\nThe following are **future commands**, not commands claimed to pass in this planning PR:\n\n```sh\ncd clients/flutter\ndart format --output=none --set-exit-if-changed .\nflutter analyze\nflutter test\nflutter build apk --debug\nflutter test integration_test -d <test-device-id>\nflutter install --debug -d <test-device-id>\n```\n\nPin SDK/toolchains when P1 starts, record `flutter doctor -v`, commit the app lockfile and review package\nlicences. Provide versioned CI debug APK artifacts from a stable development application ID/key plus\ncommit/checksum/install instructions; keep production keys out of source and all retained signing keys out of untrusted PR jobs.\nA protected distribution workflow or local build with the retained test key supplies upgradeable\nartifacts; ordinary untrusted PR builds compile/test without those secrets.\nTest an upgrade without uninstalling/wiping. Production signed APK/AAB and store admission are separate\nfrom debug acceptance; release builds must reject cleartext/invalid TLS by default.\n\nAndroid USB proposal: after installing ADB, `adb reverse tcp:8080 tcp:8080` can forward the phone's\nloopback endpoint to the existing host test instance. Validate the browser/login poll and returned\ncanonical Nextcloud URL as part of the real test. A phone/emulator's `127.0.0.1` alone is not this host.\nPermit loopback cleartext only in explicit debug configuration; never disable certificate verification.\nFor Wi-Fi/iPhone use a configured reachable test origin and approved trusted-domain/proxy settings.\nDo not expose or reset the test instance in this planning PR.\n\niOS source support is a target, but physical iPhone installation needs macOS/Xcode and provisioning;\n`TestFlight` needs the relevant Apple team/program setup. A Linux APK build or unsigned simulator build\nis not iPhone acceptance. If iPhone is the chosen first device, P1 must establish that install path\nbefore claiming a usable first delivery. Keep all secrets in protected signing storage.\n\nEach PR runs affected Flutter unit/widget/integration tests, Rust contract/migration tests and existing\nNextcloud regressions, plus the repository's complete mandatory gate. Use a phone and a second phone\nor real Nextcloud browser as distinct authenticated household clients; mocked transports do not replace\nend-to-end proof. Record OS/device/build, conditions, screenshots using synthetic data and results,\nincluding pending unsupported capabilities. Do not commit personal credentials or health fixtures.\n\n## Decisions and approval gates\n\n| Decision | Proposed treatment / owner | Required by |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| First physical phone/platform | Accepted: Android APK plus a real Android emulator; explicit customer Go received | Before P1 implementation |\n| Install origin/signing | Test setup with customer-controlled reachability and keys; no hostname baked into client | P1 |\n| Shared vs individual plans | Shared household default with per-person alternatives; preserve separate-plan extension | P2 model review |\n| Sensitive/child profile access and retention | Explicit policy/projections before any diagnosis fields or health-cache sync | P2 |\n| OCR/provider support | Prefer on-device; validate package/platform/licence; external service requires separate consent | P5 |\n| Notification/push capabilities | Local deadline reminders first with measured limits; no assumed provider | P4 |\n| Standalone/hosted identity and commercial distribution | Keep open in F18/F19/F30, not silently implemented as master tokens in the app | Separate accepted slice |\n\n## Source-pack coverage\n\nPhase 0 → this audit/plan; shell → P1; tour/recipes/activity (original phases 1/7) → P2;\nplanning/mealprep/pantry (2/4) → P3; cooking (6) → P4; capture (5) → P5; complete shopping (3) → P1.\nThe five source journeys map to P2+P3 (mixed dietary rules), P3 (Thursday swap and six portions),\nP5 (uncertain photo import) and P1 (two-client offline list). None is treated as implemented by import.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0035_flutter_mobile_client_plan_md {}

#[doc = "# Flutter mobile client and smartphone delivery\n\nStatus: In progress\nPriority: Must\nOrigin: Customer, 2026-11-13; supplied product specification dated 2026-11-12\nMilestone: M1\n\n## User value and approval boundary\n\nUse Mealshop on a real smartphone from the first implementation PR, initially against the existing\nNextcloud installation. Prefer a few substantial, complete user journeys over separate scaffolding,\nbackend-only and screen-only PRs. Each delivery extends an installable app.\n\nThe customer approved Android APK delivery, explicitly requested an Android emulator, and gave the\nimplementation Go on 2026-11-13. P1 is now in progress on `story/flutter-pocket-shopping`.\nThe earlier planning PR remains a separate review record; its preserved source import is unchanged.\n\nThe [original pack](https://github.com/Th3Link/mealshop/blob/main/references/mobile-product-spec-2026-11-12/README.md) remains a preserved\nreference. [Current state](../page_specs_0035_flutter_mobile_client_current_state_md/index.html) distinguishes shipped server/web behaviour from missing\nmobile functionality. [The plan](../page_specs_0035_flutter_mobile_client_plan_md/index.html) proposes **five larger implementation PRs**, each containing\nits required backend, Flutter UI, tests and phone-install instructions. Internal tasks remain small;\nthere is no extra technical-foundation PR before the first usable app.\n\n## Acceptance contract\n\n1. **Install and connect (P1).** An installable development build connects to a configurable Nextcloud\n   base URL, authenticates with that device's revocable app credential, selects/creates a household,\n   exposes the current role and supports sign-out/revocation/account switching without cross-account\n   cache leakage. Real phone connectivity and update installation are demonstrated. Android APK is\n   the accepted initial platform; a real accelerated Android emulator is required in addition to a\n   downloadable handset-installable build. Physical-handset testing is recorded separately.\n2. **Independent shopping (P1).** Manual exact-quantity entry, editing/removal, check-off/undo,\n   source details, shops/order and existing product capture work without a meal plan. Two authorized\n   clients see canonical changes. Bounded durable offline add/check operations survive process death,\n   show pending/failed state and replay without duplicate purchases or entries. Changed contribution\n   scope, concurrent edits and revoked membership require safe reconciliation, not blind overwrite.\n3. **People and content (P2).** A skippable, resumable tour creates two people with different explicit\n   dietary rules, distinguishes persons from login accounts, and separates hard exclusions from soft\n   preferences. Presets/exceptions and optional goals/windows/prep preferences have visible effective\n   rules; every introduced hard rule is enforced on the server's existing evaluation/planning paths.\n   Sensitive health fields require an approved access/retention model before collection. Recipes,\n   ingredients, subrecipes/homemade inputs, exact nutrition uncertainty, collections and sharing work\n   through existing contracts. Optional activity records duration/type without requiring weight.\n4. **Plan and prepare (P3).** The server proposes a reviewed household week with per-meal attendees,\n   portions, substitutions and explicit infeasibility. Hard exclusions are never relaxed. A Thursday\n   swap previews only relevant shopping changes and preserves manual/purchased amounts. Six physical\n   prepared portions can allocate four to later meals and retain two as explicitly stored leftovers;\n   planned allocations alone never prove cooked stock or create invented storage/safety guarantees.\n5. **Cook and ferment (P4).** Guided cooking, step ingredients, simultaneous timers, multi-day baking,\n   preparation calendar, brew recipes/batches/equipment/readings and completion/history/learning have\n   native phone workflows. Server deadlines persist; cached cooking remains readable offline. Local\n   reminders are permission-aware and reconcile on resume/restart without resetting deadlines or\n   claiming guaranteed delivery. Disconnected actions are not reported as server-confirmed.\n6. **Capture and review (P5).** Share-sheet URLs, manual recipe entry, supported barcode scanning and\n   on-device OCR candidates lead to explicit source/ingredient/quantity review. Unknown units or\n   nutrition stay unresolved. Imported sharing remains source-link-only across server and mobile\n   cache/export/share surfaces. Restricted video downloads and external OCR/AI uploads are not assumed.\n7. **Quality across P1–P5.** DE/EN keyed messages ship from P1 with English canonical code/content,\n   exact decimal-string quantities and source-language fallback. Each active screen has loading,\n   empty, error, offline/conflict and appropriate reader states, accessible touch/semantics and text\n   scaling. Real-device evidence, release/test artifact identity, upgrade test, domain/API tests and\n   current-head CI accompany each PR. No sensitive records, credentials or screenshots enter CI logs.\n\n## Scope reconciliation\n\nThe five-tab target is Today / Plan / Shopping / Recipes / More. Enable a tab when its real workflow\nships; do not fill the initial build with dead or dummy destinations. The first launch opens Shopping.\nSolo use follows the same journey with one person; additional accounts/profiles are not mandatory.\nShared household planning is proposed, with per-person attendance/alternatives; independent personal\nplans remain an explicit later extension. No irreversible model decision is inferred from the pack.\n\nNextcloud is the first working connection, reusing its account and household authority. Standalone\nhosted authentication, Git/SQL adapters, commercial admission and federation retain F18/F19/F20/F30\nscope and are not prerequisites for a useful Nextcloud phone app. Unsupported deployment modes are\nidentified honestly. Flutter localization contributes to F29 without declaring its full cross-client\nand versioned-content contract Done.\n\nOptional medical context is not a diagnosis-to-diet engine. Smart scales, wearables, autonomous\npurchasing and restricted video retrieval remain explicit non-goals. Nutrition/energy estimates\nneed defensible inputs and uncertainty, not clinical claims or mandatory calorie tracking.\n\n## Approval and traceability\n\nReview [plan.md](../page_specs_0035_flutter_mobile_client_plan_md/index.html), [ux-notes.md](../page_specs_0035_flutter_mobile_client_ux_notes_md/index.html), [adrs.md](../page_specs_0035_flutter_mobile_client_adrs_md/index.html) and proposed ADR 0026.\nN01/N03/N04/N06–N10 apply. F18 AC4 and the Flutter part of F29 are related contracts, not closed by\nthis planning PR. All implementation checklist entries remain unchecked until delivered and verified.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0035_flutter_mobile_client_specification_md {}

#[doc = "# Smartphone interaction plan\n\nStatus: Accepted P1 direction; implementation and emulator verification in progress. The ZIP's UX is a target;\nthis document reconciles it with existing data and the five complete deliveries.\n\n## Navigation and the first useful launch\n\nTarget bottom destinations: Today / Plan / Shopping / Recipes / More. P1 starts with Shopping/More,\nP2 adds Recipes, P3 activates Today/Plan. Preserve selected household and destination safely across\nrelaunch; never mix caches across accounts. No disabled “coming soon” tabs or decorative empty screens.\n\nUse adaptive Flutter controls and platform back/navigation conventions, accessible touch targets,\ntext scaling, screen-reader semantics, high-contrast light/dark surfaces and reduced-motion behaviour.\nUse a small coherent token set; the phone app is not the Vue screen embedded in a `WebView`. Keep the\nexisting Nextcloud client's native components/styles unchanged except where contract compatibility\nrequires changes. Every shipped action has loading, empty, error, pending/offline and conflict states.\n\n## Daily shopping first (P1)\n\nOpen the last authorized household; a visible switcher allows changing it. Fast text add with clear\nquantity/unit input and optional ingredient/product selection; large check targets, separate purchased\nsection and reachable undo. Details retain exact manual/recipe/plan contributions and provenance.\n\nDisplay the last server sync time and pending count. Optimistic check-off has a visible pending state;\n“purchased” is confirmed only after the canonical server response/receipt. A failed or conflicted write\nkeeps the entry/draft and explains reconciliation. Airplane-mode process restart retains the outbox.\nDo not turn a check of an old amount into a purchase of newly added unseen requirements.\n\n## People and content (P2)\n\nThe tour asks one or two questions per step, saves a protected local draft, supports optional skip and\nreturns to an editable derived-rule summary. Hard exclusions, soft dislikes and source uncertainty use\ntext/icons, not colour alone. Presets with exceptions display their actual meaning. An own-egg allowance\ncannot waive an unrelated allergy or treat unknown provenance as known.\n\nKeep sensitive medical context optional and hidden until its access/retention contract is approved.\nOptional profile avatars never replace accessible person names. Solo users need no extra account.\nNo required diagnosis/weight/calorie target. Activity entry remains a small optional personal log.\n\nRecipes have compact always-open ingredient/part/step composition, inline ingredient creation, explicit\nhomemade outputs and retained exact original quantities. Source/ranged/unknown nutrition is visible.\nIncoming shared content follows server projections; imported material offers its source link only.\n\n## Plan, prepare and cook (P3–P4)\n\nToday shows real chronological meals, participants and next preparation/cooking action. Plan uses a\nweek strip plus a selected-day list for breakfast/lunch/snack/dinner; per-person skips and portion edits\nare explicit. Review shopping deltas and infeasibility before committing changes. Batch allocation\nexplains actual produced/available/allocated/remaining quantities, not just planned meals.\n\nCooking uses large steps with their linked ingredients, persistent independent timers and meaningful\npause/complete/reschedule actions. Offline cached content identifies its freshness. Canonical server\nstate, pending local actions and local reminder delivery remain distinct. Notification denial leaves a\nusable workflow and an explanation of actual limitations. Brewing keeps explicit equipment completion.\n\n## Capture and locale (P5; locale from P1)\n\nCamera/share-sheet content enters review before save. Retain original source/candidates next to reviewed\nfields; highlight unknown units/ingredient mapping and allow manual fallback. Permission cancellation\nreturns to the prior context with its draft intact. No automatic restricted-video retrieval.\n\nEnglish is the code/canonical base; DE/EN UI ships in P1, with device-language normalization, a clear\nmanual choice and documented fallback. Search includes localized aliases. Switching locale must not\nreinterpret in-progress numbers; decimal strings and original unit/source precision remain exact.\nRespect safe areas, keyboard insets and one-handed use without hiding required review actions.\n\n## Phone acceptance per delivery\n\nEach release includes synthetic normal/error/offline/conflict screens, smallest supported width and\nlarge-font checks, screen-reader/keyboard focus where applicable, reader-role screenshots and actual\nphone OS/build evidence. Exercise interrupted drafts, account switches and denied permissions. Mocked\nwidgets and screenshots supplement physical-device journeys; they do not prove device installation,\ncamera access, background notifications or offline replay by themselves.\n\nQuality targets: at least 48×48 logical-pixel touch areas, 4.5:1 normal text/control contrast,\n320-logical-pixel layouts with 200% text scaling, and actual `TalkBack`/`VoiceOver` checks for the\nchosen platforms. Validate these alongside conflict/permission states, not just happy-path screenshots.\n[Flutter accessibility guidance](https://docs.flutter.dev/ui/accessibility) supports this proposed bar;\nno mobile conformance is claimed by this plan.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0035_flutter_mobile_client_ux_notes_md {}

#[doc = "# F35 verification\n\n## Historical planning PR evidence\n\nThe following section records the earlier planning-only PR at commit 77b6cd5. It is not the\nimplementation status after the customer Go; current P1 evidence is tracked below.\n\nScope: imported source documents, source-based capability audit, proposed delivery/UX/ADR and navigation\nlinks. No Flutter application, new API behaviour, SDK setup, device build or mobile runtime acceptance\nis claimed. Existing test-instance data and deployment configuration were not accessed or changed.\n\n## Import and consistency checks\n\n- The seven extracted files match the customer ZIP byte for byte; `manifest.json` records each length\n  and SHA-256 plus the original archive hash. Only the agent reference filename changes.\n- Root `AGENTS.md` matches its pre-import checksum. No nested active `AGENTS.md` is imported.\n- Relative links in the changed planning/index/reference documents resolve locally.\n- Current-state claims use actual Rust routes/models and current Nextcloud/MCP client transport code.\n  Required mobile capabilities are explicitly proposed rather than labelled implemented.\n- F35 and ADR 0026 remain Draft/Proposed. Existing F18/F29/F30 requirements retain their status and\n  unchecked work. The client folder does not exist; all implementation tasks are still unchecked.\n- The only executable-source change is generated rustdoc metadata. No Flutter/domain implementation,\n  pipeline change or test-instance mutation is included.\n\n## Mandatory security-gate maintenance\n\nThe initial `cargo audit` refreshed the advisory database and found three issues in the pre-existing\nlockfile: `RUSTSEC-2026-0523` and `RUSTSEC-2026-0524` in `quinn-proto 0.11.18`, and\n`RUSTSEC-2026-0538` in `quinn-udp 0.5.15`. The official `RustSec` records specify patched versions\n`quinn-proto >=0.11.19` and `quinn-udp >=0.5.16,<0.6.0` (or the separate newer minor branch).\n\nUse a separate maintenance commit for the minimal generated lockfile updates to **0.11.19 / 0.5.16**.\nCargo also refreshes existing Windows-target dependency edges; no direct manifest, feature selection,\nnew crate, advisory ignore or licence exception is added. `cargo tree --locked -i quinn-proto` reports\nno active reverse dependency for the current host/features; that does not waive the whole-lock audit.\nNo application or phone behaviour is inferred from a passing security gate.\n\nPrimary records were read from the refreshed official advisory checkout (origin\n`https://github.com/RustSec/advisory-db.git`):\n\n- [RUSTSEC-2026-0523](https://github.com/RustSec/advisory-db/blob/main/crates/quinn-proto/RUSTSEC-2026-0523.md)\n- [RUSTSEC-2026-0524](https://github.com/RustSec/advisory-db/blob/main/crates/quinn-proto/RUSTSEC-2026-0524.md)\n- [RUSTSEC-2026-0538](https://github.com/RustSec/advisory-db/blob/main/crates/quinn-udp/RUSTSEC-2026-0538.md)\n\n## Publication checks\n\nRun the complete required repository gate after the patch updates, plus generated-doc synchronization,\nstrict rustdoc and the import/link/status checks above. Record actual command/results in the PR; final\nhead CI must pass before handoff. A passing Rust/docs pipeline does not establish Flutter functionality.\nPhysical-phone build, installation, two-client offline and OS notification proof belong to P1–P5.\n\n## P1 implementation evidence\n\nP1 implementation is in this PR; F35 remains **In progress** for P2–P5 and the physical-handset\nacceptance. No handset is attached. Android APKs and a working visible accelerated emulator are\nprovided; emulator evidence is not relabelled as physical-phone evidence.\n\n### Automated gates\n\n- Full required catalogue/import/verifier/i18n/fmt/Clippy/nextest/licence/advisory gate; strict rustdoc\n  and generated-document synchronization. The suite now contains **186 Rust tests**, including five\n  mobile receipt/group tests: restart/replay, concurrent duplicate check, authority removal, stale\n  contribution scope, expiry/capacity/corrupt receipts, purchase-only-new-source and legacy projection.\n- Flutter format and strict analysis; **19 unit/widget tests** cover exact localized input, original\n  precision, anonymous Login Flow polling, origin/prefix/redirect boundaries, frozen outbox after\n  lost/malformed responses, durable-write failure, revocation, explicit first household choice,\n  household removal while a draft is open, restart and local purchase state.\n- Real API 36 Android integration through `python3 scripts/mobile.py integration`: two named native\n  tests (plus framework teardown) pass. They exercise the Android Keystore/atomic-file adapter and\n  native German shopping/navigation with synthetic HTTP transport; this is separate from live login.\n- Owner/reader shopping and connection at **320 dp and 200% text** in DE/EN; Android 48-dp tap target\n  and labelled-target guidelines, group labels, pending checkbox semantics and error layout pass.\n  These checks do not claim a manual `TalkBack` audit or complete WCAG certification.\n- Existing Nextcloud client: **36 Vitest tests**, production type-check/build, npm audit (no\n  vulnerabilities), and **five shopping Playwright tests** against the actual test instance pass.\n- `python3 scripts/verify_mobile_packages.py --audit`: 53 locked package licence records; 45 external\n  Pub package versions, no matched OSV advisories. The built APK includes the root AGPL notice.\n- The seven imported ZIP records still match byte for byte; root `AGENTS.md` retains its original hash.\n\n### Live Android / Nextcloud session\n\nEnvironment: Nextcloud **35.0.2**, `AppAPI` **35**, own Google APIs Android 16/API 36 r07 Pixel 6 AVD,\nEmulator 37.2.13.0, KVM and local hardware GPU, system Chrome **133.0.6943.137**. `SwiftShader` triggered\nan independently traced guest OpenGL-pipe deadlock/system-server watchdog on this NVIDIA host; the\nhelper supports `--host-gpu` without clearing AVD data. CI uses its own software-rendered guest.\n\nThe following checks use only the ledger-owned synthetic `flutter-p1` household; retained customer\nhousehold directories are never inspected, copied or used as fixtures. Browser authentication is\noperated using field positions and fixed button labels only; no authentication screenshot, raw\nbrowser URL, poll token or app password is retained in evidence.\n\n1. Enter the configured loopback origin in the native app, launch Login Flow v2 in system Chrome,\n   submit the authorized test account in that browser, grant device access and return to Mealshop.\n   Choose the own synthetic household. The app uses the resulting device credential through the\n   real `index.php/apps/app_api/proxy/mealshop` front controller, never the `ExApp` secret.\n2. Add **200.000001 g** natively. Compare the live legacy proxy snapshot: original quantity and\n   remaining quantity retain every decimal digit. Native purchase and undo each match server state.\n3. Remove only the emulator's port reverse, force-stop and restart the app. Last household and\n   encrypted cached list remain. Add a separate **2 pcs** entry offline, check that draft locally,\n   queue a check for the earlier item, force-stop/restart again and confirm the pending checkbox.\n   The server still has only the original source while disconnected.\n4. Change the original source to **250.000001 g** from a second authenticated proxy client. Restore\n   the reverse and refresh natively. Only the new draft's 2 pcs are purchased; changed original\n   demand remains entirely unpurchased, with a visible conflict. Explicit native review/confirmation\n   then purchases the reviewed 250.000001 g. No blind rebase or duplicate source occurs.\n\nNetwork loss above is simulated by removing ADB reverse forwarding; it is not a claim of an airplane-mode\nOS test. Lost-response replay/restart and permission revocation are additionally proved by executable\nserver/controller tests. Manual product entry/shops reuse the existing server contracts; consented\nOpen Food Facts lookup remains dependent on the external service. Camera capture, background sync,\nproduction signing, iOS, physical handset/`TalkBack`/performance profiling and P2–P5 are not claimed.\n"]
